75 billion to below $750 billion\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined capital expenditures are at least $675 billion and below $750 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 675000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 750000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"$750 billion or more\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined capital expenditures are at least $750 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 750000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i256\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\",\n    \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\",\n     \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\",\n     \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\",\n     \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i232\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"A Circuit Board Problem Just Delayed Nvidia's Next AI System to 2028 And Chip Stocks Are Already Feeling the Fallout\",\n    \"passage\": \"2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Alphabet / Google\",\n     \"what\": \"capital expenditure guidance\",\n     \"how_much\": \"up to $190bn\",\n     \"period\": \"2026\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast (guidance)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i233\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"A Circuit Board Problem Just Delayed Nvidia's Next AI System to 2028 And Chip Stocks Are Already Feeling the Fallout\",\n    \"passage\": \"Google Cloud revenue rose 63% with backlog nearly doubling to over $460 billion\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Google Cloud\",\n     \"what\": \"revenue growth and backlog\",\n     \"how_much\": \"revenue +63%; backlog nearly doubled to over $460bn\",\n     \"period\": \"latest reported quarter\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i295\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-10\",\n    \"title\": \"Here are Friday's biggest analyst calls: Nvidia, SpaceX, Toll, Shopify, Twilio, Seagate, Chipotle & more\",\n    \"passage\": \"the company describing \\\"accelerating growth rates\\\" even as revenues approach the $100 bn per quarter mark\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA management, relayed by Morgan Stanley\",\n     \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\",\n     \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source The four largest AI hyperscalers ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] The four largest AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\",\n   \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source The four largest AI hyperscalers ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] The four largest AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e95 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management projected hyperscaler spending of $650 billion in 2026.\\n    Quote: after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e47; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e130 [third_party_view; Allen Harris; original source Goldman Sachs ; from gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512 2026-07-06] Goldman Sachs estimated annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026\",\n   \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source The four largest AI hyperscalers ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] The four largest AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95, e184; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e184 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author estimates that the four largest AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e47, e192; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e192 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author said AI hyperscalers planned $650 billion of data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e184; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e205 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Google ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Google guided 2026 capital expenditures to $190 billion.\\n    Quote: 2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion.\",\n   \"- e316 [third_party_view; GuruFocus; original source GuruFocus ; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] Analysts expect overall AI capital expenditures by major cloud service providers to rise significantly, even as NVIDIA's share of Meta's spending may decline.\\n    Quote: However, analysts remain optimistic about NVIDIA's future, suggesting that while its share within Meta may decline, overall AI capital expenditures from major cloud service providers are expected to rise significantly.\",\n   \"- e353 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source tech-insider.org 2026-07-12; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron reportedly sold out their 2026 HBM output to AI data-center customers.\\n    Quote: The cause is a global memory shortage: Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron have reportedly sold out their 2026 HBM output to AI data center customers.\",\n   \"- e358 [third_party_view; tech-insider.org, reporting Micron and Kearney’s PERLab; original source Micron and Kearney’s PERLab ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Micron suggested memory supply may not meaningfully normalize until 2027 and may gradually return to balance by 2028; Kearney’s PERLab reportedly projected the shortage could last into 2030.\\n    Quote: Micron has since suggested supply may not meaningfully normalize until 2027, with a gradual return to balance by 2028, while other forecasters take a bleaker view: an analysis from Kearney’s PERLab reportedly projects the shortage could persist into 2030 .\",\n   \"- e421 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Meta raised its 2026 capital expenditure plan to $125–145 billion and launched Meta Compute, a service to rent excess internal AI capacity to enterprises.\\n    Quote: Meta raised 2026 capex to $125 to $145 billion, then quietly launched Meta Compute, a service renting its excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e233 (2026-07-01); both are in force: Bloomberg reported that Meta was setting up a cloud-based business to sell AI compute and models on July 1, 2026.\",\n   \"- e421 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Meta raised its 2026 capital expenditure plan to $125–145 billion and launched Meta Compute, a service to rent excess internal AI capacity to enterprises.\\n    Quote: Meta raised 2026 capex to $125 to $145 billion, then quietly launched Meta Compute, a service renting its excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e460; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e233 (2026-07-01); both are in force: Bloomberg reported that Meta was setting up a cloud-based business to sell AI compute and models on July 1, 2026.\",\n   \"- e434 [third_party_view; fool.com author Justin Pope; original source Meta Platforms, Microsoft, Alphabet and Amazon ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] The author says Meta Platforms, Microsoft, Alphabet and Amazon are planning higher capital expenditures in calendar 2026; no amount is given.\\n    Quote: Hyperscalers, including Meta Platforms , Microsoft , Alphabet , and Amazon , are planning higher capital expenditures in 2026.\",\n   \"- e435 [third_party_view; fool.com author Justin Pope; original source Goldman Sachs ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] Goldman Sachs estimates AI compute spending at approximately $494 billion in calendar 2026, rising to $1.13 trillion by 2031.\\n    Quote: Goldman Sachs estimates that AI compute spending will grow from approximately $494 billion this year to $1.13 trillion by 2031.\",\n   \"- e460 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja 2026-07-14; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] The author cited Meta’s $145 billion infrastructure budget, partly aimed at custom silicon, as a potential competitive threat to NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: The Reddit crowd has fixated on competitive threats, from DeepSeek’s rumored in-house chip to Meta’s $145B infrastructure budget aimed partly at custom silicon.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e421; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e472 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois), quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the AI-factory buildout was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: Jensen Huang framed the moment bluntly: “The buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e481; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e481 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja), quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said AI factory buildout was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: “The buildout of AI factories , the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e472; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e502 [fact; EBC; original source Amazon ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Amazon borrowed another $25 billion; EBC said the borrowing caused a minor selloff in AI-related debt.\\n    Quote: Amazon recently made headlines by borrowing another $25 billion, causing a minor selloff in AI-related debt .\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 13,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Below $700 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $700 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 700000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$800 billion to below $900 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 900000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$900 billion to below $1000 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 900000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 1000000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$1000 billion or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 1000000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v7\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Combined data-center capital expenditures of the four largest AI hyperscalers\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-02-29\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \