",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-04\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA revenue growth forecast\",\n     \"how_much\": \"82% this year; 41% next year\",\n     \"period\": \"this year and next year (fiscal or calendar both accepted, D233)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i143\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n    \"passage\": \"Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"unnamed estimates\",\n     \"what\": \"memory's share of data center spend\",\n     \"how_much\": \"about half\",\n     \"period\": \"2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i161\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"CAPITAL IDEAS: The lag 7 — Is Micron the new Nvidia?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Goldman Sachs estimate\",\n     \"what\": \"annual AI infrastructure capex (chips, data centers, power, cooling, networking)\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$765B (2026); $1.6T (2031); ~$7.6T cumulative 2026-2031\",\n     \"period\": \"2026; 2031; 2026-2031\",\n     \"condition\": \"could reach\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e48 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] NVIDIA projects that the four largest AI hyperscalers’ combined data-center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\",\n   \"- e48 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] NVIDIA projects that the four largest AI hyperscalers’ combined data-center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e94; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e94 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management forecast that hyperscaler spending would exceed $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e48; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e94 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management forecast that hyperscaler spending would exceed $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e48, e185; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e185 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] NVIDIA claims the four largest AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e94, e193; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e193 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimated AI hyperscalers’ data-center capital expenditures could exceed $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e185; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e185 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] NVIDIA claims the four largest AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e94, e193, e347; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e347 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] NVIDIA told investors it expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to exceed $1 trillion next year; the item does not specify the spending population or calendar/fiscal basis.\\n    Quote: However, Nvidia told investors last quarter that it expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to rise to over $1 trillion next year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e185; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e193 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimated AI hyperscalers’ data-center capital expenditures could exceed $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e185, e426; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e426 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Morgan Stanley forecast that Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta will spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure and add 19.5 GW of compute capacity in calendar 2027; Google is forecast to add 6.8 GW. The article says the four added roughly 6.7 GW in 2025.\\n    Quote: The analyst says Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta are forecast to spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure next year, adding 19.5 gigawatts (GW) of incremental compute capacity. In 2025, they added roughly 6.7 GW. Google alone will add 6.8 GW, or more than the hyperscalers did combined two years ago.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e193; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e472 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois), quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the AI-factory buildout was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: Jensen Huang framed the moment bluntly: “The buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e481; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e481 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja), quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said AI factory buildout was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: “The buildout of AI factories , the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e472; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n[\n {\n  \"control\": 14,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Rubin Ultra generation, in Kyber NVL144 racks, by December 31, 2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has begun shipping Rubin Ultra systems by December 31, 2027.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not begun shipping Rubin Ultra systems by December 31, 2027.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v8\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA launch its Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by December 31, 2028?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture launch\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2028\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA launches the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture on or before December 31, 2028.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"No\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not launched the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by December 31, 2028.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i100\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis (a research firm's report, not NVIDIA)\",\n     \"what\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack for Vera Rubin Ultra delayed; cause: PCB midplane manufacturability\",\n     \"how_much\": \"more than 12 months\",\n     \"period\": \"from 2027 to 2028\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i179\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 reportedly pushed back more than a year, Asian suppliers drop\",\n    \"passage\": \"The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled. Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"four-die Rubin Ultra cancelled; two-die version remains\",\n     \"how_much\": \"roughly half the real-world compute\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\",\n     \"status_note\": \"cancelled\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i181\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 reportedly pushed back more than a year, Asian suppliers drop\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis, about NVIDIA's plan\",\n     \"what\": \"sell more Oberon-Rubin racks to cover the Kyber gap\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\",\n     \"status_note\": \"as claimed\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i101\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Our roadmap is intact\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"rejects the SemiAnalysis report; says its roadmap (Rubin Ultra / Kyber in 2027) is unchanged\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i197\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\",\n    \"passage\": \"An Nvidia representative responded with a short statement to Tom's Hardware : \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA representative\",\n     \"what\": \"denies the report: roadmap intact\",\n     \"condition\": \"unclear whether the original or an already updated roadmap is meant\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e55 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber rack-scale architecture, designed for Rubin Ultra chips, has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis\",\n   \"- e56 [party_statement; CNBC, quoting NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remains intact, rejecting SemiAnalysis’s report of a Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\",\n   \"- e57 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said Kyber NVL144 is delayed to 2028 because its PCB midplane remains difficult to manufacture.\\n    Quote: \\\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\\\" the firm said\",\n   \"- e58 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA’s NVL576 system, which links eight racks via optical connections, is likely delayed or limited to small volumes.\\n    Quote: NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.\",\n   \"- e59 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA scrapped a backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together after cloud service providers and hyperscalers objected to the design and operating burden.\\n    Quote: A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \\\"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\\\" SemiAnalysis said.\",\n   \"- e60 [third_party_view; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA has no proven solution to expand Rubin Ultra’s scale-up system size and predicted this could give AMD and Google a technical opening in the high-end market.\\n    Quote: That leaves Nvidia with \\\"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\\\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.\",\n   \"- e55 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber rack-scale architecture, designed for Rubin Ultra chips, has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e70, e149, e159; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e56 [party_statement; CNBC, quoting NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remains intact, rejecting SemiAnalysis’s report of a Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e72; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e57 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said Kyber NVL144 is delayed to 2028 because its PCB midplane remains difficult to manufacture.\\n    Quote: \\\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\\\" the firm said\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e89, e138, e143; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e58 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA’s NVL576 system, which links eight racks via optical connections, is likely delayed or limited to small volumes.\\n    Quote: NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e91, e151; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e59 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA scrapped a backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together after cloud service providers and hyperscalers objected to the design and operating burden.\\n    Quote: A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \\\"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\\\" SemiAnalysis said.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e71, e90, e152, e153; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e70 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA’s Rubin Ultra high-density rack design was delayed by more than 12 months, citing persistent manufacturing problems with its complex PCB midplane.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis claims the high-density rack design built for Rubin Ultra GPUs has slipped by more than 12 months. The firm blamed persistent manufacturing problems with the system's complex PCB midplane.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e55; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e71 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed NVIDIA scrapped its NVL72x2 back-to-back rack after hyperscaler customers pushed back.\\n    Quote: The firm also claimed Nvidia scrapped its NVL72x2 back-to-back rack after pushback from hyperscaler customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e59, e160, e161; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e72 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] NVIDIA told media outlets that its product roadmap remains intact, rejecting claims of delays and a scrapped rack design.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the claims, telling media outlets that its roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e56, e93; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e89 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com, reporting SemiAnalysis’s claim; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack architecture had been delayed to 2028 because of PCB midplane manufacturing challenges.\\n    Quote: “Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,” SemiAnalysis said\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e57, e150; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e90 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com, reporting SemiAnalysis’s claim; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA scrapped its alternative plan to place two Oberon racks back-to-back after cloud companies and hyperscalers objected to the design and operational burden.\\n    Quote: Nvidia’s alternative plan, which involved placing two Oberon racks back-to-back in order to achieve a similar power output, has also been scrapped after cloud companies and hyperscalers pushed back against its “odd design and heavy operational burden.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e59, e145; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e91 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com, reporting SemiAnalysis’s claim; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said manufacturing issues would likely delay NVIDIA’s planned NVL576 system or limit it to small volumes.\\n    Quote: The manufacturing issues will also impact the planned NVL576 system, which connects 8x Oberon racks over CPO between the NVSwitches, meaning that the system will also likely be delayed or limited to small volumes, the firm noted.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e58; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e92 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com, reporting SemiAnalysis’s claim; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis had reported that NVIDIA canceled its four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of a two-chiplet design because of manufacturing execution concerns.\\n    Quote: The news comes a week after SemiAnalysis separately reported that Nvidia had canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of the two-chiplet design, also due to “manufacturing execution concerns.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e140, e164; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e93 [party_statement; NVIDIA spokesperson, quoted by datacenterdynamics.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-06; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] An NVIDIA spokesperson said the company’s roadmap was intact in response to questions about the Kyber claims.\\n    Quote: In response to a request for comment from DCD regarding the Kyber claims, a spokesperson for Nvidia said: \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e72, e144, e158; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e138 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack system has been delayed by more than 12 months, to 2028, because of manufacturing problems.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's next AI server rack system, Kyber NVL144, has been pushed back more than twelve months to 2028 because of manufacturing problems.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e57, e157; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e140 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA canceled the planned four-compute-die version of Rubin Ultra.\\n    Quote: The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92, e146; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e141 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that only the two-die Rubin Ultra version remains, with roughly half the real-world compute performance of the canceled four-die version.\\n    Quote: Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\",\n   \"- e142 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s CPO-NVSwitch interconnect technology will not arrive until the Feynman generation, the generation after next.\\n    Quote: A key interconnect technology called CPO-NVSwitch, which links many chips into a single large system, won't arrive until the generation after next, called Feynman.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e165; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e143 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack architecture will be delayed to 2028 because of PCB midplane manufacturing challenges.\\n    Quote: Supply chain research firm SemiAnalysis claimed in a weekend report that Nvidia's highly anticipated Kyber NVL144 rack architecture will be delayed to 2028 due to manufacturing challenges with its PCB midplane.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e57; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e144 [party_statement; An NVIDIA spokesperson; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-06; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] An NVIDIA spokesperson said the company's product roadmap was intact, denying the reported Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: An Nvidia spokesperson swiftly refuted such claims in a brief statement emailed to Investing.com, stating: \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e93; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e145 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis alleged that NVIDIA cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design after operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.\\n    Quote: The research firm further alleged that Nvidia cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design following heavy operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e90; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e146 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed that NVIDIA scrapped a four-die configuration of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform in favor of a downsized version.\\n    Quote: Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e140; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e147 [third_party_view; Investing.com, relaying analysts cited by Bloomberg; original source Analysts cited by Bloomberg ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Analysts cited by Bloomberg said the rumored setbacks could severely limit NVIDIA's future hardware scale-up capacity and create a competitive opening for AMD's MI500X and Broadcom-backed custom TPUs.\\n    Quote: According to analysts cited by Bloomberg, these rumored technical setbacks could severely cap the scale-up capacity of Nvidia's future hardware. This perceived vulnerability may create a wider competitive window for alternative AI platforms, specifically AMD's MI500X and Broadcom-backed custom TPUs.\",\n   \"- e149 [third_party_view; tikr.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber rack-scale server design has been delayed from 2027 to 2028.\\n    Quote: Research firm SemiAnalysis reported that Kyber, Nvidia’s next rack-scale server design, has been pushed back more than a year , from 2027 to 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e55; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e150 [third_party_view; tikr.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis attributed the Kyber delay to manufacturing problems with a specialized circuit board.\\n    Quote: The holdup comes down to manufacturing problems with a specialized circuit board inside the system, according to SemiAnalysis.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e89; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e151 [third_party_view; tikr.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA’s NVL576 system is likely to be delayed or ship only in small volumes.\\n    Quote: A larger version, called NVL576, which links eight racks together via optical connections, is also likely to be delayed or to ship only in small volumes.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e58, e162; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e152 [third_party_view; tikr.com; original source NVIDIA, as reported by SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] NVIDIA scrapped a backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together to provide similar computing power.\\n    Quote: Nvidia had a backup plan: bolting two current-generation racks together to achieve similar power, but that idea was scrapped too.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e59; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e153 [rumour; tikr.com; original source Cloud customers, as reported by SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] Cloud customers reportedly rejected NVIDIA’s two-rack backup design, citing its awkward design and high operating cost.\\n    Quote: Cloud customers reportedly rejected it because the design was awkward and the service was expensive to run.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e59; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e157 [rumour; businesstimes.com.sg; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c0432377817a1c00a1bbadf0 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 faced printed-circuit-board construction setbacks, contributing to a reported delay of more than a year.\\n    Quote: Research firm SemiAnalysis said in an X post that Nvidia’s Kyber NVL144 hit setbacks in the construction of printed circuit boards for the platform.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e138; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e158 [party_statement; NVIDIA representative, in a statement to Tom's Hardware on 2026-07-06; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-06; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] NVIDIA said its roadmap remains intact, without clarifying whether it meant the original or an updated roadmap.\\n    Quote: \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e93; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e159 [rumour; Tom's Hardware, reporting SemiAnalysis's thread on X; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reportedly said NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 rack, intended for 2027 Rubin Ultra GPUs, would not ship until 2028—a delay of more than 12 months.\\n    Quote: Nvidia reportedly won't ship its Kyber NVL144 rack until 2028, a delay of more than 12 months that pushes the cabinet meant for 2027's Rubin Ultra GPUs into the following year, according to a SemiAnalysis thread on X.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e55; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e160 [rumour; Tom's Hardware, reporting claims attributed later in the item to SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reportedly cancelled the NVL72x2 stopgap rack, leaving no proven alternative to expand Rubin Ultra scale-up in 2027.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is also understood to have killed NVL72x2, a stopgap rack designed to tide customers over, and that no proven alternative is now available to widen Rubin Ultra's scale-up in 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e71; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e161 [rumour; Tom's Hardware, reporting SemiAnalysis's account; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA abandoned its NVL72x2 stopgap after its largest customers objected to operating two linked Oberon cabinets as one unit.\\n    Quote: NVL72x2 would have bolted two Oberon racks back-to-back to reach Kyber-class density over copper NVLink, per SemiAnalysis, which said Nvidia abandoned the stopgap after its largest customers balked at running two linked cabinets as a single unit.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e71; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e162 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware; original source Tom's Hardware 2026-07-06; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] Tom's Hardware reported that NVIDIA's NVL576 configuration may be delayed or ship in low volume until co-packaged optics mature.\\n    Quote: NVL576, a separate configuration tying eight racks together through co-packaged optics, is likely to slip too or ship in low volume until that optical technology matures.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e151; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e163 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware; original source Tom's Hardware 2026-07-06; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] Tom's Hardware assessed that NVIDIA had no proven way to expand Rubin Ultra scale-up, so its largest single domain in 2027 could be no larger than Oberon's.\\n    Quote: These cancellations leave Nvidia with \\\"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\\\" meaning the largest single Rubin Ultra domain in 2027 could match, but not exceed, what Oberon already delivers.\",\n   \"- e164 [rumour; Tom's Hardware; original source Tom's Hardware ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reportedly changed Rubin Ultra from a quad-chiplet GPU to a dual-chiplet part last week, halving per-package compute, because of manufacturing execution concerns.\\n    Quote: Nvidia dropped the quad-chiplet Rubin Ultra GPU for a dual-chiplet part last week over manufacturing execution concerns, halving the accelerator's per-package compute.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e92; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e165 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware, reporting SemiAnalysis's estimate; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reportedly estimated that a fully production-ready co-packaged-optics NVSwitch would not arrive before the Feynman generation after Rubin, leaving copper as the near-term option for linking Rubin Ultra racks.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis has also placed a fully production-ready co-packaged optics NVSwitch no earlier than the Feynman generation that follows Rubin, which leaves copper as the only near-term solution for linking Rubin Ultra at rack scale and thereby puts even more weight on the PCB midplane.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e142; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e56 [party_statement; CNBC, quoting NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remains intact, rejecting SemiAnalysis’s report of a Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e72, e183; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e58 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA’s NVL576 system, which links eight racks via optical connections, is likely delayed or limited to small volumes.\\n    Quote: NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e91, e151, e198; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e70 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA’s Rubin Ultra high-density rack design was delayed by more than 12 months, citing persistent manufacturing problems with its complex PCB midplane.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis claims the high-density rack design built for Rubin Ultra GPUs has slipped by more than 12 months. The firm blamed persistent manufacturing problems with the system's complex PCB midplane.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e55, e182; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e72 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] NVIDIA told media outlets that its product roadmap remains intact, rejecting claims of delays and a scrapped rack design.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected th