remains intact, rejecting SemiAnalysis’s report of a Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e72, e183, e268, e383; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e382 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack system could be delayed until 2028 because of manufacturing problems with a crucial circuit board.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis reported that its Kyber NVL144 next-gen AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 due to troubles with manufacturing a crucial circuit board.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e143; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e383 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remains intact despite the reported possible Kyber NVL144 delay.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has come out and said its roadmap remains intact\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e56; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e268 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA (denial and roadmap statement); barchart.com (2027 launch expectation) ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] NVIDIA denied reports of a Kyber delay and said its roadmap remains on track; the author said Kyber, designed for Rubin Ultra, is expected to launch in 2027.\\n    Quote: company denied the speculation, maintaining that its roadmap remains on track. Designed for the Rubin Ultra platform, Kyber is expected to launch in 2027 as an integrated AI infrastructure system\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e56, e337, e391; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"