n\": \"Chinese authorities publicly authorize at least one Chinese company to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"Chinese authorities have not publicly authorized any Chinese company to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v9\",\n   \"question\": \"Will China officially authorize AI firms to import NVIDIA H200 chips by December 31, 2026?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"China's H200 import-approval process\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2026\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"condition\": \"China officially authorizes AI firms to import NVIDIA H200 chips by 2026-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"No\",\n    \"condition\": \"China has not officially authorized AI firms to import NVIDIA H200 chips by 2026-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i270\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-08\",\n    \"title\": \"China to let AI firms buy Nvidia H200s, says report\",\n    \"passage\": \"China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Chinese officials\",\n     \"what\": \"permission for top AI companies (Alibaba, ByteDance, DeepSeek) to buy NVIDIA H200 chips, each on approval stating the number and reason\",\n     \"how_much\": \"a limited amount; total may be fewer than 200,000\",\n     \"condition\": \"approval per request; limited amount\",\n     \"status\": \"rumour\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i304\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-14\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia slashes list of authorized customers in Asia in a bid to reduce AI chip smuggling, report claims — company sent field inspectors, called customers to check if business is genuine after pressure from Washington\",\n    \"passage\": \"Beijing refused to allow Chinese companies to buy these AI processors\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Beijing\",\n     \"what\": \"Chinese companies not allowed to buy NVIDIA H200\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i305\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-14\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia slashes list of authorized customers in Asia in a bid to reduce AI chip smuggling, report claims — company sent field inspectors, called customers to check if business is genuine after pressure from Washington\",\n    \"passage\": \"all domestic suppliers are sold out and that they’re even considering less powerful chips\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"unnamed Chinese tech executive\",\n     \"what\": \"China's domestic AI-chip suppliers are sold out; buyers are considering less powerful chips\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i309\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-14\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia slashes list of authorized customers in Asia in a bid to reduce AI chip smuggling, report claims — company sent field inspectors, called customers to check if business is genuine after pressure from Washington\",\n    \"passage\": \"President Donald Trump took a 180-degree turn in December 2025 and finally allowed Nvidia to export its H200 GPUs to select customers in the region\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"US President Trump\",\n     \"what\": \"allowed H200 exports to select customers in China\",\n     \"period\": \"December 2025\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e222 [rumour; straitstimes.com; original source The Information 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] The Information reported on July 8, citing unnamed sources, that Chinese officials told Alibaba, ByteDance and DeepSeek they could seek approval to buy limited quantities of NVIDIA H200 chips, subject to stating the quantity and reason for purchase.\\n    Quote: China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia, a sign the country is easing restrictions on the coveted US technology, according to the Information news site. Chinese officials have informed companies such as Alibaba Group, ByteDance and DeepSeek that they will have permission to purchase some of the processors, which are used to devel\",\n   \"- e223 [rumour; straitstimes.com; original source The Information 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] The Information reported on July 8, citing unnamed sources, that China was still determining the permitted H200 purchase quantity and the total could be fewer than 200,000 chips.\\n    Quote: The Chinese government, meanwhile, is still figuring out how many H200 chips to allow the companies to buy, but the total may end up being fewer than 200,000, the Information reported.\",\n   \"- e222 [rumour; straitstimes.com; original source The Information 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] The Information reported on July 8, citing unnamed sources, that Chinese officials told Alibaba, ByteDance and DeepSeek they could seek approval to buy limited quantities of NVIDIA H200 chips, subject to stating the quantity and reason for purchase.\\n    Quote: China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia, a sign the country is easing restrictions on the coveted US technology, according to the Information news site. Chinese officials have informed companies such as Alibaba Group, ByteDance and DeepSeek that they will have permission to purchase some of the processors, which are used to devel\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e284, e301; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e284 [rumour; technologyreview.com; original source China ; from gnews:50a84fa6b2f3eb33f29948a4 2026-07-09] China reportedly plans to permit Alibaba, ByteDance and DeepSeek to buy NVIDIA H200 chips; no date or quantity was given.\\n    Quote: China plans to let its top AI firms buy Nvidia H200 chips\",\n   \"- e285 [rumour; South China Morning Post; original source An unnamed source with knowledge of the matter ; from gnews:91684b863d274b10246d0c13 2026-07-09] An unnamed source said China’s government plans to let selected companies, including Alibaba, buy limited numbers of NVIDIA H200 chips; no date or quantity was specified.\\n    Quote: Now, however, China’s stance is beginning to change, as the government plans to let selected companies – including Alibaba Group Holding – buy limited numbers of the device, a source with knowledge of the matter told the South China Morning Post.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e284; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e301 [fact; moomoo.com; original source China ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] China is moving to grant limited approval for domestic firms to buy NVIDIA H200 processors, with firms required to seek individual approval for quantities and use cases.\\n    Quote: The stock is also navigating a complex geopolitical environment as China moves to grant limited approval for domestic firms to purchase H200 processors. While this policy shift eases access to Nvidia’s technology, companies must now request individual approval for specific quantities and use cases.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e222; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e320 [third_party_view; David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA management (outlook assumption); David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St. (upside interpretation) ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA's Q2 FY2027 revenue outlook assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China; the author says a policy change permitting H200 exports could add upside.\\n    Quote: Notably, that outlook assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China, meaning any policy thaw on H200 exports could represent additional upside.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e313; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e320 [third_party_view; David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St.; original source NVIDIA management (outlook assumption); David Moadel / 24/7 Wall St. (upside interpretation) ; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] NVIDIA's Q2 FY2027 revenue outlook assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China; the author says a policy change permitting H200 exports could add upside.\\n    Quote: Notably, that outlook assumed zero Data Center compute revenue from China, meaning any policy thaw on H200 exports could represent additional upside.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e313, e410; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e430 [party_statement; Jeffery Kessler; original source Jeffery Kessler, Under Secretary of Commerce for Industry and Security 2026-07-14; from gnews:9d898f2bf43ed52a98e1587a 2026-07-14] Under Secretary of Commerce for Industry and Security Jeffery Kessler said that very few NVIDIA H200 and equivalent chips had shipped to China and Hong Kong under licenses; he gave no shipment amount or period.\\n    Quote: The bottom line is very few shipments against licenses for H200s and equivalents have taken place. It's a very small quantity of chips,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e452, e499; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e431 [party_statement; Jeffery Kessler; original source Jeffery Kessler, Under Secretary of Commerce for Industry and Security 2026-07-14; from gnews:9d898f2bf43ed52a98e1587a 2026-07-14] Jeffery Kessler said the U.S. government assesses H200 license applications case by case, requiring applicants to meet national security requirements and submit to compliance inspections.\\n    Quote: Kessler said that the U.S. government assessed companies that want the H200 chips on a case-by-case basis, with applicants needing to meet national security requirements and submit to inspections to make sure the chips are compliant.\",\n   \"- e432 [party_statement; Jeffery Kessler; original source Jeffery Kessler, Under Secretary of Commerce for Industry and Security 2026-07-14; from gnews:9d898f2bf43ed52a98e1587a 2026-07-14] Jeffery Kessler said the U.S. government denies some applications for H200 export licenses; he gave no number of denials.\\n    Quote: There are cases where we deny the license applications we receive,\",\n   \"- e452 [party_statement; Yahoo Finance; original source A top U.S. commerce official ; from gnews:c73b90b63a733c6ab712fcdd 2026-07-14] A top U.S. commerce official told Congress that NVIDIA H200 chip shipments to China had begun, with very few shipped so far.\\n    Quote: Separately, a top U.S. commerce official told Congress that while the number of H200 chips shipped to China so far was \\\"very few,\\\" the shipments have commenced.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e430; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e468 [fact; Tom's Hardware; original source Beijing ; from gnews:2a41a34c16f5280b624481fb 2026-07-14] China has refused to allow Chinese companies to buy NVIDIA H200 GPUs and is relying on domestic semiconductor manufacturers to fill the gap.\\n    Quote: However, Beijing refused to allow Chinese companies to buy these AI processors — instead, it’s banking on domestic semiconductor manufacturers to make up for the shortfall, but it’s apparently still not enough.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e223 (2026-07-08); both are in force: The Information reported on July 8, citing unnamed sources, that China was still determining the permitted H200 purchase quantity and the total could be fewer than 200,000 chips.\",\n   \"- e486 [fact; Reuters; original source U.S. authorities ; from gnews:24268bfaab6ef1d7876b188c 2026-07-14] The U.S. permitted ZTE Kangxun Telecom and server maker Maginfra to purchase NVIDIA H200 chips; the item gives no approval date or purchase amount.\\n    Quote: ZTE Kangxun Telecom and server maker Maginfra have been permitted to purchase Nvidia's H200 chips\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e497; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e487 [rumour; Reuters; original source Unnamed sources familiar with the matter ; from gnews:24268bfaab6ef1d7876b188c 2026-07-14] Unnamed sources said some Chinese cloud firms recently told partners and clients they may soon be able to obtain H200 chips, indicating progress in Chinese authorities' import reviews.\\n    Quote: some Chinese cloud firms have recently told partners and clients they may soon be able to obtain H200 chips, the sources said, indicating some progress in import reviews by Chinese authorities.\",\n   \"- e497 [fact; Tom's Hardware; original source The U.S. government 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] The U.S. approved ZTE and Maginfra to buy NVIDIA H200 chips; the item reports the approval on 2026-07-14.\\n    Quote: Today, Reuters reports that Chinese telecoms giant ZTE and server firm Maginfra have received U.S. approval to buy Nvidia's last-gen H200 \\\"Hopper\\\" chips.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e486; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e498 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware, recounting Reuters; original source Reuters ; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] Reuters reported that Chinese technology firms had more than two million NVIDIA H200 chips on order about six months before 2026-07-14, exceeding NVIDIA's available supply at the time.\\n    Quote: But even with those domestic production initiatives, the Chinese hunger for AI silicon is so deep that six months ago, Reuters said the nation's tech firms had more than two million H200 chips on order, far more than what Nvidia had on hand at the time.\",\n   \"- e499 [party_statement; Tom's Hardware, quoting CNBC's account of a U.S. trade official's remarks; original source A U.S. trade official 2026-07-14; from gnews:3221eba2826b001b12b82770 2026-07-14] A U.S. trade official said that very few H200 and equivalent chips had shipped against licenses, describing the quantity as very small, on 2026-07-14.\\n    Quote: CNBC cites a U.S. trade official who today stated that \\\"very few shipments against licenses for H200s and equivalents have taken place. It’s a very small quantity of chips\\\" during a congressional hearing.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e430; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 16,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a guarantee of OpenAI's Ohio data-center lease by 2027-06-30?\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-06-30\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has signed the guarantee by the due day.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"It has not.\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v2\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a financial guarantee for OpenAI’s lease of the large Ohio data center by 2027-07-01?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"NVIDIA guarantee for OpenAI’s Ohio data-center lease\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-07-01\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has signed a financial guarantee for OpenAI’s Ohio data-center lease by 2027-07-01.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"No\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not signed a financial guarantee for OpenAI’s Ohio data-center lease by 2027-07-01.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i005\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.\",\n    \"passage\": \"NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA (per The Information)\",\n     \"what\": \"negotiating to guarantee OpenAI's lease of a large Ohio data center\",\n     \"how_much\": \"the data center could cost as much as $500 billion if fully built (asset cost, not the guarantee amount)\",\n     \"condition\": \"in negotiation; nothing signed\",\n     \"status\": \"rumour\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i006\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.\",\n    \"passage\": \"NVIDIA subsequently added another $3.5 billion to guarantee customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"guarantees of customer data center leases, in exchange for rights to buy their shares\",\n     \"how_much\": \"an additional $3.5 billion\",\n     \"period\": \"quarter ended April 2026 (filed May)\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i116\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia is diving even deeper, as it has started backstopping datacenter leases\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA backstops datacenter leases for neoclouds (a second kind of obligation)\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i119\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia’s backstop program is only getting started, and we see announcements coming faster every quarter. Many Neoclouds are already deep in negotiations with Nvidia\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"more NVIDIA backstops exist but are not public; many neoclouds in negotiation; announcements accelerating\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\",\n     \"status_note\": \"existing undisclosed backstops; more deals are a forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e2 [rumour; moomoo.com, relaying The Information; original source The Information ; from gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45 2026-07-01] The Information reported that NVIDIA was negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large Ohio data center; the article said full build-out could cost as much as $500 billion.\\n    Quote: According to prior reporting by The Information, NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio—an asset that, if fully built out at current prices for chips, labor, power, and other materials, could cost as much as $500 billion.\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 17,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026?\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"Nvidia has begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v3\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Vera Rubin platform by 2026-12-31?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Whether NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin platform begins shipping by year-end 2026.\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2026\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has begun shipping the Vera Rubin platform by 2026-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"No\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not begun shipping the Vera Rubin platform by 2026-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i105\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin systems in full production; shipping to eight cloud partners including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud\",\n     \"period\": \"this fall (2026)\",\n     \"status\": \"happened (full production); plan (shipping this fall)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i219\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\",\n     \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i202\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia's 2026 Rubin GPUs, which reuse the current Oberon rack, aren't part of the reported delay.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Tom's Hardware\",\n     \"what\": \"scope of the reported delay: Rubin Ultra/Kyber only; 2026 Rubin on Oberon unaffected\",\n     \"period\": \"2026\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i207\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Delays Next-Generation Kyber Server Architecture as Manufacturing Hurdles Give Rivals a Rare Opening\",\n    \"passage\": \"the company’s current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and set to start shipping this fall to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA (as restated)\",\n     \"what\": \"Rubin systems in full production; first shipments to eight cloud partners incl. AWS, Azure, Google Cloud\",\n     \"period\": \"this fall\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\",\n     \"status_note\": \"in full production; shipping this fall is a plan\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e21 [third_party_view; fool.com; original source fool.com 2026-07-02; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The author says NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform is in full production and could begin shipping in 2026.\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year.\",\n   \"- e22 [party_statement; fool.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\",\n   \"- e59 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and are scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\",\n   \"- e62 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] NVIDIA plans to launch its first stand-alone CPU this fall as part of the Vera Rubin platform.\\n    Quote: In fact, it's launching its first-ever stand-alone CPU this fall as part of the Vera Rubin platform.\",\n   \"- e59 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and are scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e146; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e79 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley Research estimated that a Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack would cost hyperscale cloud providers about $7.8 million per unit, versus about $4 million for a GB300 NVL72 rack.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley Research estimates that Nvidia 's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers around $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation.\",\n   \"- e80 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated NVIDIA would charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when sold in volume.\\n    Quote: The bank estimates Nvidia will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when sold in volume.\",\n   \"- e81 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated memory content at about $2 million per Vera Rubin rack, up 435% from the prior generation, including 54 terabytes of LPDDR5X and roughly $1 million or more of 3D NAND storage.\\n    Quote: Morgan Stanley puts memory content per rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND storage that was virtually absent from earlier systems.\",\n   \"- e82 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments are scheduled for Q3 2026, with volume ramping in Q4.\\n    Quote: First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n   \"- e83 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source Morgan Stanley Research ; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] Morgan Stanley estimated memory's share of the bill of materials increased from 5–10% on GB200 to 25–30% on VR200, while the GPU share declined from about 63% to 51%.\\n    Quote: As a share of the bill of materials, memory rose from 5 to 10 percent on the GB200 to 25 to 30 percent on the VR200, while the GPU's share fell from roughly 63 percent to 51 percent.\",\n   \"- e97 [third_party_view; 247WallSt, reporting; original source Unidentified reports cited by 247WallSt ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Reports say NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems are delayed; the item gives no revised schedule.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA shares are under pressure on reports of delays across their upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems.\",\n   \"- e146 [party_statement; tikr.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] NVIDIA’s current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and are scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight major cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: company’s current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and set to start shipping this fall to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e59; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e302 [third_party_view; Vandita Jadeja, 247Wallst.com; original source Vandita Jadeja, 247Wallst.com 2026-07-10; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] The author says a path to $300 requires Blackwell Ultra and Vera Rubin to ship on schedule, gross margins to remain at 75%, and a sovereign or hyperscaler deal to be upsized.\\n    Quote: Three things need to go right: Blackwell Ultra and Vera Rubin ship on schedule, gross margins hold the 75% line, and one sovereign or hyperscaler deal gets upsized in a headline print.\",\n   \"- e361 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA launched its Vera Rubin AI platform, according to the article.\\n    Quote: Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform\",\n   \"- e362 [rumour; en.sedaily.com; original source LG Electronics' Production Research Institute, as reported by en.sedaily.com citing the semiconductor industry ; from gnews:bf96def37a9c3a5f19f5d43c 2026-07-12] LG Electronics' Production Research Institute completed an AI server rack prototype matching NVIDIA Vera Rubin compute-tray specifications in the first half of 2026.\\n    Quote: LG Electronics' Production Research Institute (PRI) completed development of an AI server rack prototype matching the compute tray specifications of Nvidia's \\\"Vera Rubin\\\" in the first half of the year.\",\n   \"- e363 [rumour; en.sedaily.com; original source LG Electronics, as reported by en.sedaily.com citing the semiconductor industry ; from gnews:bf96def37a9c3a5f19f5d43c 2026-07-12] LG Electronics plans to seek orders from global big tech companies after second-half 2026 reliability evaluations and begin mass production of its NVIDIA Vera Rubin-specification AI server rack in 2027.\\n    Quote: LG plans to secure orders from global big tech companies after reliability evaluations in the second half and begin mass production next year.\",\n   \"- e409 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source Milk Road AI ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Milk Road AI estimates that rack costs for one GW of AI infrastructure using Nvidia Vera Rubin reach $25 billion.\\n    Quote: Under Vera Rubin, rack costs jump to $25 billion.\",\n   \"- e59 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and are scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e146, e468; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e438 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois) 2026-07-14; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA's Blackwell 300 was ramping, with the Vera Rubin platform queued to follow.\\n    Quote: Blackwell 300 is ramping, and the Vera Rubin platform is queued behind it.\",\n   \"- e468 [third_party_view; ebc.com; original source ebc.com ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] The article reported that NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin architecture remained officially on track for late-2026 shipping.\\n    Quote: Blackwell Ultra and Rubin: Target shipping dates for Blackwell Ultra chips are ramping up fast and the Vera Rubin architecture remains officially on track for late 2026, but the market is currently priced for absolute perfection.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e59; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n[\n {\n  \"control\": 19,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"What will Nvidia's total revenue be in FY2028?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-02-28\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $650 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 650000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $550 billion and below $650 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 550000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 650000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $480 billion and below $550 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 480000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 550000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is at least $420 billion and below $480 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 420000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 480000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"FY2028 total revenue is below $420 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 420000000000.0\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v5\",\n   \"question\": \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2028?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"NVIDIA total revenue in FY2028.\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-02-28\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2028\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at least $609.4 billion, 10% or more above the cited $554 billion estimate.\",\n    \"lo\": 609400000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at least $554 billion and below $609.4 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 554000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 609400000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at least $498.6 billion and below $554 billion, within 10% below the cited estimate.\",\n    \"lo\": 498600000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 554000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is at least $443.2 billion and below $498.6 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 443200000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 498600000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"Total revenue is below $443.2 billion, more than 20% below the cited estimate.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 443200000000.0\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i037\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-02\",\n    \"title\": \"Microsoft vs. Nvidia: Which Is the Better AI Stock to Own for the Next 3 Years?\",\n    \"passage\": \"from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA total revenue estimates\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$392 billion this fiscal year, $554 billion next year (from $253 billion trailing twelve months)\",\n     \"period\": \"this fiscal year (FY2027) and the following year (FY2028)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i256\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\",\n    \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\",\n     \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\",\n     \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\",\n     \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i079\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-03\",\n    \"title\": \"Here's What a $25,000 Investment in Nvidia Could Be Worth if History Repeats Itself\",\n    \"passage\": \"In March, CEO Jensen Huang said he expects the company's Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales between that time and the end of 2027\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Jensen Huang\",\n     \"what\": \"Blackwell and Vera Rubin sales\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$1 trillion\",\n     \"period\": \"March 2026 to end-2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i100\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis (a research firm's report, not NVIDIA)\",\n     \"what\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack for Vera Rubin Ultra delayed; cause: PCB midplane manufacturability\",\n     \"how_much\": \"more than 12 months\",\n     \"period\": \"from 2027 to 2028\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e23 [third_party_view; fool.com; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of $392 billion in FY2027, versus $253 billion in trailing-12-month revenue cited as the starting point.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\",\n   \"- e31 [fact; sdxcentral.com; original source Microsoft and MediaTek ; from gnews:1740f3733eedc34d8bac9b65 2026-07-03] Microsoft and MediaTek plan to launch microLED-based data center networking interconnects for partners by late 2027.\\n    Quote: The pair plans to launch microLED-based data center networking interconnects for partners by late 2027 .\",\n   \"- e37 [third_party_view; Jim Cramer, as quoted from Mad Money by Yahoo Finance; original source Jim Cramer ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Jim Cramer said Google and Amazon, both NVIDIA customers, claim to have better chips than NVIDIA and feel NVIDIA charges too much.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's got an insane amount of business. So what's keeping a lid on the stock? Well, the company has some powerful detractors, mainly clients that feel they charge too much, like Google and Amazon and Tesla. Hey, by the way, they're customers. The first two claim that they have better chips than NVIDIA, even as they use NVIDIA.\",\n   \"- e38 [third_party_view; Jim Cramer, as quoted from Mad Money by Yahoo Finance; original source Jim Cramer ; from gnews:a96a4cbf6aae35d01d0d285b 2026-07-03] Jim Cramer said Broadcom CEO Hock Tan has said Broadcom can compete with NVIDIA and take share from it.\\n    Quote: Plus, there's Broadcom, vicious competitor, and CEO Hock Tan's out there saying it can compete; it can take share from NVIDIA.\",\n   \"- e44 [party_statement; Josh Parker, quoted by Jonathan Sayers; original source Josh Parker, head of corporate sustainability at NVIDIA ; from gnews:a8fab49de53d125314a6688a 2026-07-04] NVIDIA corporate sustainability head Josh Parker said AI-compute demand driving data-center construction is growing faster than almost any other infrastructure-investment category; no period was specified.\\n    Quote: AI workloads are not getting lighter. The compute demand driving data center construction is growing faster than almost any other category of infrastructure investment.\",\n   \"- e46 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] NVIDIA projects that the four largest AI hyperscalers' data-center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\",\n   \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project NVIDIA revenue growth of 82% in 2026 and 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\",\n   \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] Wall Street analysts project NVIDIA revenue growth of 82% in 2026 and 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year, so there's another external source that's projecting even more growth for Nvidia.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e91; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e91 [third_party_view; fool.com (Keithen Drury); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA revenue growth of 82% for the rest of 2026 and 41% in 2027.\\n    Quote: For the rest of this year, they expect 82% growth. For 2027, that figure rises to 41%.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e47; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e96 [third_party_view; TradingView; original source Zacks ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] Zacks consensus estimates call for NVIDIA revenue and earnings to grow in FY2027 and FY2028.\\n    Quote: The Zacks Consensus Estimate points to continued revenue and earnings growth in both fiscal 2027 and fiscal 2028, suggesting that demand for NVIDIA's AI products remains far from slowing.\",\n   \"- e108 [third_party_view; 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance; original source 247WallSt, author Danielle Liverance 2026-07-06; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] The author says demand looks strong in 2027 but raises the possibility that NVIDIA growth slows dramatically in 2028 as hyperscalers turn to debt and equity offerings.\\n    Quote: Demand looks strong in 2027, but with hyperscalers now having to move into debt and equity offerings, the question of whether growth slows dramatically in 2028 is now front and center on investors minds.\",\n   \"- e141 [party_statement; Investing.com, relaying Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry management 2026-07-03; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] Hon Hai management forecast continued acceleration in AI demand; Mizuho analyst Jordan Klein said this was a positive sign ahead of NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin rack launch.\\n    Quote: Klein noted that Hon Hai management forecasted a continued acceleration in AI demand, which the analyst said was \\\"a very good sign into the NVDA launch of their new Vera Rubin rack.\\\"\",\n   \"- e46 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] NVIDIA projects that the four largest AI hyperscalers' data-center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e174; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e174 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] NVIDIA claims the four largest AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e46; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e176 [third_party_view; fool.com (author Jack Delaney); original source fool.com (author Jack Delaney) 2026-07-07; from gnews:9026c944c63575a080ce7ba9 2026-07-07] The author says NVIDIA is set to be an initial hardware supplier for SpaceX's planned orbital data centers; no amount or timing is given.\\n    Quote: That involvement with SpaceX will expand further, as Nvidia is set to serve as an initial supplier of hardware for SpaceX's orbital data centers.\",\n   \"- e177 [party_statement; fool.com (author Jack Delaney); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:9026c944c63575a080ce7ba9 2026-07-07] NVIDIA announced that it plans to launch the Vera Rubin Space-1 Module in the future; no launch date is given.\\n    Quote: Also, Nvidia announced in March that it will be launching its Vera Rubin Space-1 Module at some point in the future.\",\n   \"- e197 [rumour; idnfinancials.com; original source Three unnamed sources cited by Reuters ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Reuters, citing three unnamed sources, reported that DeepSeek is developing chips specifically for AI inference; the project was described as a potential competitor to NVIDIA's AI chips.\\n    Quote: According to Reuters , citing three sources familiar with the plans, DeepSeek's chips are being designed specifically for inference, the stage where trained AI models generate responses for users.\",\n   \"- e198 [third_party_view; idnfinancials.com, quoting Richard Windsor; original source Richard Windsor, Radio Free Mobile ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] Analyst Richard Windsor said NVIDIA's position in China was effectively zero and would remain so, and that DeepSeek was unlikely to sell chips outside China without access to advanced manufacturing technology; he said the development would not affect NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: \\\"Nvidia's position in China is effectively at zero and will remain that way. DeepSeek has almost no chance of selling chips outside China unless it gains access to advanced manufacturing technology,\\\" said analyst Richard Windsor of Radio Free Mobile, adding that the development would not affect the chipmaker.\",\n   \"- e199 [third_party_view; idnfinancials.com; original source idnfinancials.com 2026-07-07; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] The article reported that Huawei now controls around half of China's AI chip market, valued at approximately US$50 billion.\\n    Quote: Huawei has expanded its domestic market share and now controls around half of China's AI chip market, which is valued at approximately US$50 billion.\",\n   \"- e200 [fact; idnfinancials.com; original source OpenAI and Broadcom ; from gnews:2957e5c79a365952140c8cce 2026-07-07] OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, Jalapeno, in collaboration with Broadcom in June 2026, adding a potential competitor in AI inference computing.\\n    Quote: OpenAI introduced its first inference chip, called Jalapeno, last month in collaboration with Broadcom\",\n   \"- e23 [third_party_view; fool.com; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of $392 billion in FY2027, versus $253 billion in trailing-12-month revenue cited as the starting point.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e208; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e215 [third_party_view; Futuriom, recounting Bloomberg's report; original source Bloomberg 2026-07-01; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] Bloomberg reported on July 1 that Meta is setting up a cloud-based business to sell AI compute and models.\\n    Quote: On July 1, the same day NVIDIA announced its new revenue-sharing model, Bloomberg reported that Meta is setting up a cloud-based business selling AI compute and models.\",\n   \"- e221 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com, Gerelyn Terzo; original source Earl Duke Austin, CEO of Quanta Services ; from gnews:abfc64ce8fc333f13d06a757 2026-07-08] Quanta CEO Earl Duke Austin estimated a $2.4 trillion total addressable market through 2030 from converging utility, generation, and large-load demand.\\n    Quote: Earl Duke Austin, CEO of specialty contractor Quanta, already attached a number on the opportunity: a $2.4 trillion total addressable market through 2030 from converging utility, generation, and large-load demand.\",\n   \"- e222 [fact; 247wallst.com, Gerelyn Terzo; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:abfc64ce8fc333f13d06a757 2026-07-08] The article says NVIDIA committed an unspecified amount to train plumbers and electricians.\\n    Quote: Nvidia just committed serious money to train plumbers and electricians, and the retailer that sells to those exact tradespeople responded by printing a 52-week low.\",\n   \"- e225 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence survey findings; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence said they plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they’ll allocate 46% of their budget for artificial intelligence accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% today, according to a Bloomberg Intelligence survey released on Tuesday.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e159; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e227 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence survey findings; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg Intelligence’s survey expects Nvidia’s market share in China to shrink as H20 chips become harder to find and local firms take over; Beijing has urged Chinese tech firms not to use H20 chips.\\n    Quote: While Nvidia’s products remain popular, the Santa Clara-based firm’s market share is expected to shrink as its H20 chips, which Beijing has urged its tech firms not to use, become harder to find and local firms take over, according to the survey.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e161; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e228 [fact; Bloomberg; original source The Chinese government ; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) to build data centers nationwide over the next five years as part of a government-led AI expansion initiative.\\n    Quote: China is allocating roughly 2 trillion yuan ($294 billion) to build data centers across the country in the next five years, a government-led initiative to expand use of AI in sectors from healthcare to city management.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e162; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e229 [third_party_view; Bloomberg; original source Bloomberg News ; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg News reported that domestic companies will supply at least 80% of core technologies, including chips, for China’s data-center initiative.\\n    Quote: At least 80% of core technologies, such as chips, will be supplied by domestic companies, Bloomberg News reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e163; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e230 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, summarizing the report; original source The report cited by Bloomberg ; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Bloomberg’s report said a global memory-chip shortage is likely to cap growth at Chinese AI firms such as SMIC, with ChangXin Memory Technologies poised to benefit, as high-bandwidth memory supply becomes a bottleneck.\\n    Quote: But a global memory chip shortage is likely to cap the growth of Chinese AI firms like Semiconductor Manufacturing International Corp. with ChangXin Memory Technologies Inc. poised to reap the benefits. The bottlenecks are shifting from sheer computing power to securing supply of high-bandwidth memory chips that support rapid data transfer, according to the report.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e164; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e240 [rumour; Notebookcheck; original source Notebookcheck, reporting an unnamed-source claim ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] NVIDIA is reportedly planning to release RTX 50 Super series cards in 2027 instead of launching the next-generation RTX 60 series.\\n    Quote: Rather than initiate a full-blown next-gen RTX 60 series launch, Nvidia is reportedly planning to release the RTX 50 Super series cards in 2027.\",\n   \"- e241 [rumour; Moore’s Law Is Dead, as reported by Notebookcheck; original source An unnamed NVIDIA source, as relayed by Moore’s Law Is Dead ; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] An unnamed NVIDIA source told leaker Moore’s Law Is Dead that NVIDIA’s RTX 60 series GPUs are not expected to launch in 2027.\\n    Quote: One of Moore’s Law Is Dead’s Nvidia source told the leaker that they don’t think the RTX 60 series GPUs are coming out in 2027.\",\n   \"- e242 [third_party_view; Notebookcheck; original source Notebookcheck 2026-07-08; from gnews:134fc6bce6a550f5376d6f27 2026-07-08] Notebookcheck reported that AMD is expected to release RDNA 5 gaming GPUs in 2027.\\n    Quote: We have been hearing about the release timeline of the next-gen AMD and Nvidia GPUs for a while now. It is now clear that we approaching the end of the current-gen GPU lifecycle, as AMD is expected to release the RDNA 5 gaming GPUs in 2027.\",\n   \"- e252 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Unnamed experts ; from gnews:57de52b4f33b0c903d256f9e 2026-07-09] Experts say DeepSeek's chip effort is unlikely to materially affect Nvidia's near-term revenue, given China's shrinking contribution to sales, but custom silicon could gradually erode pricing power and margins.\\n    Quote: Although experts note that DeepSeek's move is unlikely to materially impact Nvidia's near-term revenue, particularly given China's shrinking contribution to Nvidia's sales, it reinforces concerns that custom silicon could gradually erode the company's pricing power and margins.\",\n   \"- e261 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management cited roughly $1 trillion of revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear customer commitments.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\",\n   \"- e268 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source Bloomberg Intelligence ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Bloomberg Intelligence projects NVIDIA will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\\n    Quote: Bloomberg Intelligence projects the company will hold 70% to 75% of the AI chip market through 2030.\",\n   \"- e269 [fact; qz.com; original source Google ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Google announced its newest custom AI chip, Ironwood, earlier in 2026.\\n    Quote: The company announced its newest version, called Ironwood, earlier this year.\",\n   \"- e270 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Andy Jassy ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2 had no spare capacity to sell and was a multibillion-dollar business growing at a 150% quarterly clip.\\n    Quote: Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said in late 2025 that Trainium2, the previous generation, had no spare capacity left to sell. He said it had grown into a multibillion-dollar business at a 150% quarterly clip.\",\n   \"- e271 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Amazon's Trainium4 could arrive later in 2026; the item reports no shipment amount or capacity.\\n    Quote: Amazon's next chip, Trainium4, which packs three times the performance of its predecessor, could arrive later this year.\",\n   \"- e272 [fact; qz.com; original source Microsoft ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Microsoft announced its Maia 200 inference chip in January 2026, and it is reaching a handful of U.S. data centers.\\n    Quote: It announced Maia 200, a chip built for that work, in January 2026, and the chip is already reaching a handful of U.S. data centers.\",\n   \"- e273 [fact; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta's MTIA 300 is in production for ranking and recommendation work.\\n    Quote: The newest version, MTIA 300, is already in production for ranking and recommendation work.\",\n   \"- e274 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta plans to build three more MTIA generations over the next two years for running generative AI models.\\n    Quote: Meta is set to build three more generations over the next two years with the purpose of running generative AI models.\",\n   \"- e275 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta's MTIA 450 is planned to arrive in early 2027.\\n    Quote: The next one, MTIA 450, arrives in early 2027, doubling how fast the chip moves data in and out of memory.\",\n   \"- e276 [third_party_view; qz.com; original source qz.com ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Meta's MTIA 500 is expected to arrive later in 2027.\\n    Quote: Its eventual successor, MTIA 500, is expected to come later next year, and pushes memory speed another 50% higher.\",\n   \"- e277 [fact; qz.com; original source OpenAI and Broadcom ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] OpenAI's partnership with Broadcom plans 10 gigawatts of custom AI chips, with installation scheduled to start in the second half of 2026 and continue through 2029; none had shipped at publication.\\n    Quote: It announced a partnership with Broadcom in October 2025 to build 10 gigawatts of custom AI chips, a measure of how much power the new chips will draw once installed. None of those chips has shipped yet. Installing them is set to begin in the second half of 2026 and run through the end of 2029.\",\n   \"- e278 [fact; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla finished designing its AI5 inference chip in April 2026 and plans to produce it at TSMC's Arizona plant and Samsung's Texas plant.\\n    Quote: Tesla finished the design of its AI5 inference chip in April 2026, according to Reuters. Production is planned at both TSMC's plant in Arizona and Samsung's plant in Texas.\",\n   \"- e279 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Tesla ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] Tesla is targeting mid-2027 for mass production of its AI5 chip.\\n    Quote: Tesla is targeting mid-2027 for mass production.\",\n   \"- e280 [fact; qz.com; original source SpaceX ; from gnews:7620a6ac8ec29bf19328a734 2026-07-09] SpaceX filed plans in May for a $55 billion Texas chip-manufacturing plant called Terafab; total investment could reach $119 billion.\\n    Quote: SpaceX, Musk's other property, filed plans in May for a $55 billion chip manufacturing plant in Texas called Terafab, Reuters reported. Total investment in the plant could reach $119 billion.\",\n   \"- e281 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Quanta ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Quanta’s June 2026 monthly sales more than doubled year over year to NT$385.19 billion; Bloomberg compiled the data.\\n    Quote: Quanta, which supplies AI servers powered by Nvidia’s GPUs, saw its monthly sales more than double to 385.19 billion New Taiwanese dollars in June from a year earlier, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.\",\n   \"- e282 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Hon Hai’s monthly sales rose 52% year over year to NT$821.8 billion in June 2026, according to Bloomberg.\\n    Quote: $HON HAI PRECISION INDUSTRY SPON GDS EACH REP 2 SHS TWD10 REG'S' (HNHPF.US)$ , Nvidia’s server assembly partner, saw a 52% surge in monthly sales in June to NT$ 821.8 billion\",\n   \"- e283 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Hon Hai Precision Industry ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] Hon Hai’s quarterly sales rose 40%, more than expected, according to Bloomberg; the quarter is not specified in the item.\\n    Quote: allowing the Taiwanese company to post a bigger-than-expected 40% surge in quarterly sales, according to Bloomberg.\",\n   \"- e294 [third_party_view; trefis.com; original source Wall Street consensus, as reported by trefis.com ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] The author reports Wall Street consensus estimates NVIDIA revenue growth of about 32% annually over the next few years.\\n    Quote: Wall Street consensus sees NVIDIA’s revenue growing about 32% a year for the next few years.\",\n   \"- e297 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:6abaf2856736877236d30f6a 2026-07-10] NVIDIA management said its Vera CPU opens a new total addressable market of $200 billion for NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: Management sees its new Vera CPU opening a “brand new $200 billion TAM for NVIDIA,” a market it has never addressed before.\",\n   \"- e303 [rumour; gurufocus.com; original source gurufocus.com ; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] The article reports rumors that major NVIDIA clients, including Meta, are shifting toward developing their own AI chips, potentially reducing NVIDIA’s share of their AI-chip demand.\\n    Quote: major clients, such as Meta, are shifting towards developing their own AI chips.\",\n   \"- e307 [third_party_view; 247Wallst.com; original source 247Wallst.com 2026-07-10; from gnews:cbb9ff1a37ebb451f9321da5 2026-07-10] 247Wallst.com argued that NVIDIA's lower forward multiple may reflect the difficulty of sustaining comparable percentage growth from FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion.\\n    Quote: A cheaper forward multiple on NVIDIA can reflect a rational market pricing in decelerating growth off an enormous revenue base. NVIDIA’s FY2026 revenue reached $215.9 billion, and sustaining comparable percentage growth becomes mathematically harder from that starting point.\",\n   \"- e311 [rumour; Engadget, reporting unnamed sources; original source Unnamed sources cited in reports ; from gnews:1e2532e32b5227ae9622524b 2026-07-10] Unnamed reports say NVIDIA is not expected to launch its next set of consumer-facing gaming GPUs until 2027.\\n    Quote: According to reports , NVIDIA isn't expected to launch its next set of consumer-facing GPUs for gamers until 2027.\",\n   \"- e313 [party_statement; theverge.com; original source SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June 2026 that SK Hynix plans to ramp up memory-chip capacity over the next five years.\\n    Quote: SK Group chairman Chey Tae-won said in June that the company plans to ramp up its memory chip capacity over the next five years\",\n   \"- e314 [third_party_view; theverge.com; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:3839887e5ca53a0cb0e7c91e 2026-07-10] Bloomberg reported that the memory shortage could last until 2030.\\n    Quote: a shortage that could last until 2030, Bloomberg reports .\",\n   \"- e46 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] NVIDIA projects that the four largest AI hyperscalers' data-center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e174, e336; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e225 [third_party_view; Bloomberg, reporting Bloomberg Intelligence survey findings; original source Bloomberg Intelligence 2026-07-07; from gnews:f3ba15f5e14b15ee61d7fddc 2026-07-08] Chinese executives surveyed by Bloomberg Intelligence said they plan to allocate 46% of their AI-accelerator budgets to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% currently.\\n    Quote: Executives in the country say they’ll allocate 46% of their budget for artificial intelligence accelerators to domestic products over the next 12 months, up from 30% today, according to a Bloomberg Intelligence survey released on Tuesday.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e159, e359; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e336 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] NVIDIA expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to exceed $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: However, Nvidia told investors last quarter that it expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to rise to over $1 trillion next year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e46; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e337 [third_party_view; Keithen Drury; original source Keithen Drury 2026-07-12; from gnews:f8f440b5020fec9773812b6e 2026-07-12] The author says market expectations are for NVIDIA to retain its growth lead for the full fiscal year, while Broadcom is narrowing the gap.\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, the market still expects Nvidia to maintain its lead for the full fiscal year, though Broadcom is starting to close the gap.\",\n   \"- e339 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Wedbush Securities ; from gnews:82472d26336e1982cf8a3eff 2026-07-12] Wedbush Securities said NVIDIA’s Vera CPU platform could expand its addressable market beyond graphics processors and create billions of dollars in additional revenue.\\n    Quote: Wedbush Securities recently argued that Nvidia's new Vera CPU platform could expand the company's total addressable market (TAM) well beyond graphics processors, opening the door to billions of dollars in additional revenue.\",\n   \"- e345 [fact; fool.com; original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix reported quarterly revenue of about $35 billion, up 198% year over year and a record.\\n    Quote: In the recent quarter, for example, the company reported revenue growth of 198% to about $35 billion dollars, a record level.\",\n   \"- e346 [fact; fool.com; original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix reported that quarterly net income rose 398% year over year.\\n    Quote: Net income soared 398%\",\n   \"- e347 [fact; fool.com; original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] SK Hynix reported a 72% operating margin for the recent quarter.\\n    Quote: operating margin came in at 72%.\",\n   \"- e348 [fact; fool.com; original source Counterpoint Research ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] Counterpoint Research reported that SK Hynix held 58% of the global HBM market at the end of the first quarter.\\n    Quote: SK Hynix held 58% share globally of the HBM market as of the end of the first quarter, according to Counterpoint Research.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e315; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e349 [fact; fool.com; original source NVIDIA and SK Hynix ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] NVIDIA and SK Hynix signed a multi-year technology partnership under which SK Hynix will supply memory for areas including AI infrastructure, personal AI and robotics.\\n    Quote: The two companies even reinforced their relationship recently, signing a multi-year technology partnership. It involves SK Hynix supplying memory across a broad range of areas, from AI infrastructure to personal AI and robotics .\",\n   \"- e350 [party_statement; Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:03c38d2fe2e6e02ba5736307 2026-07-12] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said SK Hynix had been NVIDIA's largest memory partner and would continue to be its largest memory partner.\\n    Quote: \\\"SK Hynix has been Nvidia's largest memory partner and will continue to be our largest memory partner,\\\" Nvidia chief Jensen Huang said at the time.\",\n   \"- e359 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] A Bloomberg survey found Chinese technology companies expect domestic suppliers to receive roughly 46% of their AI chip spending over the next year, versus about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: A new Bloomberg survey showed Chinese technology companies expect to allocate roughly 46% of their AI chip spending to domestic suppliers over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e225; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e174 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] NVIDIA claims the four largest AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e46, e405; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e373 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] NVIDIA expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to account for a larger share of future growth.\\n    Quote: It expects sovereign AI projects and on-premise deployments to make up a larger share of future growth as AI adoption expands.\",\n   \"- e376 [fact; gurufocus.com; original source Google and Blackstone ; from gnews:1c47fd978ef50b1d7f48cbd8 2026-07-13] Google and Blackstone are working on a new cloud venture that plans to rent Google TPU capacity to AI labs and financial firms in 2027.\\n    Quote: Google is also working with Blackstone on a new cloud venture that plans to rent TPU capacity to AI labs and financial firms next year.\",\n   \"- e399 [fact; Alex Sirois; original source Meta ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Meta launched Meta Compute, a service that rents its excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\\n    Quote: then quietly launched Meta Compute, a service renting its excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e215 (2026-07-01); both are in force: Bloomberg reported on July 1 that Meta is setting up a cloud-based business to sell AI compute and models.\",\n   \"- e406 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] The article reports that Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta added roughly 6.7 GW of compute capacity in calendar 2025, citing Morgan Stanley’s figures.\\n    Quote: In 2025, they added roughly 6.7 GW.\",\n   \"- e407 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Morgan Stanley forecasts that Google alone will add 6.8 GW of compute capacity in calendar 2027, more than the four hyperscalers added combined in 2025.\\n    Quote: Google alone will add 6.8 GW, or more than the hyperscalers did combined two years ago.\",\n   \"- e408 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source Milk Road AI ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Milk Road AI estimates that one GW of AI infrastructure costs $6–11 billion using Broadcom- or Marvell-designed ASIC racks, versus roughly $19 billion using Nvidia GB300-based racks.\\n    Quote: Milk Road AI estimates that building one gigawatt of AI infrastructure using Broadcom- or Marvell-designed ASIC racks cost between $6 billion and $11 billion, compared with roughly $19 billion using Nvidia GB300-based racks.\",\n   \"- e409 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source Milk Road AI ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Milk Road AI estimates that rack costs for one GW of AI infrastructure using Nvidia Vera Rubin reach $25 billion.\\n    Quote: Under Vera Rubin, rack costs jump to $25 billion.\",\n   \"- e23 [third_party_view; fool.com; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of $392 billion in FY2027, versus $253 billion in trailing-12-month revenue cited as the starting point.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia's business could double over the next couple of years, from trailing-12-month revenue of $253 billion to $392 billion this fiscal year, and $554 billion the following year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e208, e417; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e261 [party_statement; fool.com (Adam Spatacco); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:931ee0196ca609e637235fad 2026-07-09] NVIDIA management cited roughly $1 trillion of revenue visibility for Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear customer commitments.\\n    Quote: Management has also articulated roughly $1 trillion in revenue visibility for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin processors across 2026 and 2027, anchored by multiyear commitments from hyperscalers and large enterprise customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e416; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e416 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said revenue from the Blackwell and Rubin platforms could reach at least $1 trillion cumulatively through the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has said that he sees at least $1 trillion in revenue from Nvidia's Blackwell and Rubin platforms through the end of 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e261; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e417 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] Wall Street analysts estimate NVIDIA total revenue of approximately $555 billion in FY2028, ending January 2028.\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts estimate that Nvidia will generate approximately $555 billion in revenue for the company's next fiscal year, ending January 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e23; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e421 [party_statement; sg.finance.yahoo.com; original source Nokia 2026-07-15; from gnews:e153ff10e5adda87a52745a4 2026-07-14] Nokia said its jointly developed AI-driven radio access network hardware will become available to operators in 2027; it expects the platform to double data transmission over the same airwaves by 2028.\\n    Quote: The new gear will allow telecommunication network operators to transmit double the amount of data over the same airwaves by 2028, Nokia said in a statement on Wednesday. Next year, when the hardware will become available to operators, spectrum efficiency gains are expected to reach 50%, while currently 20% have been achieved.\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 20,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Below $700 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $700 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 700000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$800 billion to below $900 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 900000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$900 billion to below $1000 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 900000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 1000000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$1000 billion or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 1000000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v10\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Calendar-year data center capital expenditures by the four largest AI hyperscalers\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Lowest\",\n    \"condition\": \"The total is less than $800 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Low\",\n    \"condition\": \"The total is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 900000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Middle\",\n    \"condition\": \"The total is at least $900 billion and less than $1 trillion.\",\n    \"lo\": 900000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 1000000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"High\",\n    \"condition\": \"The total is at least $1 trillion and less than $1.1 trillion.\",\n    \"lo\": 1000000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 1100000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Highest\",\n    \"condition\": \"The total is at least $1.1 trillion.\",\n    \"lo\": 1100000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i256\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\",\n    \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\",\n     \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\",\n     \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\",\n     \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i090\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-04\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA revenue growth forecast\",\n     \"how_much\": \"82% this year; 41% next year\",\n     \"period\": \"this year and next year (fiscal or calendar both accepted, D233)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i143\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n    \"passage\": \"Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"unnamed estimates\",\n     \"what\": \"memory's share of data center spend\",\n     \"how_much\": \"about half\",\n     \"period\": \"2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i161\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"CAPITAL IDEAS: The lag 7 — Is Micron the new Nvidia?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Goldman Sachs estimate\",\n     \"what\": \"annual AI infrastructure capex (chips, data centers, power, cooling, networking)\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$765B (2026); $1.6T (2031); ~$7.6T cumulative 2026-2031\",\n     \"period\": \"2026; 2031; 2026-2031\",\n     \"condition\": \"could reach\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e174 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] NVIDIA claims the four largest AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e46; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e179 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author says AI hyperscalers plan $650 billion in data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026 and estimates the figure could exceed $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e173; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e336 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] NVIDIA expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to exceed $1 trillion in 2027.\\n    Quote: However, Nvidia told investors last quarter that it expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to rise to over $1 trillion next year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e46; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e174 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] NVIDIA claims the four largest AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e46, e405; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e405 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Morgan Stanley forecasts that Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta will spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure and add 19.5 GW of incremental compute capacity in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: The analyst says Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta are forecast to spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure next year, adding 19.5 gigawatts (GW) of incremental compute capacity.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e174; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e407 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Morgan Stanley forecasts that Google alone will add 6.8 GW of compute capacity in calendar 2027, more than the four hyperscalers added combined in 2025.\\n    Quote: Google alone will add 6.8 GW, or more than the hyperscalers did combined two years ago.\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 21,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Rubin Ultra generation, in Kyber NVL144 racks, by December 31, 2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has begun shipping Rubin Ultra systems by December 31, 2027.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not begun shipping Rubin Ultra systems by December 31, 2027.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v6\",\n   \"question\": \"By 2028-12-31, will NVIDIA launch its Kyber rack-scale architecture?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Kyber rack-scale architecture launch\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2028\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA launches Kyber on or before 2028-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"No\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not launched Kyber by 2028-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i100\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis (a research firm's report, not NVIDIA)\",\n     \"what\": \"Kyber NVL144 rack for Vera Rubin Ultra delayed; cause: PCB midplane manufacturability\",\n     \"how_much\": \"more than 12 months\",\n     \"period\": \"from 2027 to 2028\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i179\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 reportedly pushed back more than a year, Asian suppliers drop\",\n    \"passage\": \"The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled. Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"four-die Rubin Ultra cancelled; two-die version remains\",\n     \"how_much\": \"roughly half the real-world compute\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\",\n     \"status_note\": \"cancelled\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i181\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber NVL144 reportedly pushed back more than a year, Asian suppliers drop\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis, about NVIDIA's plan\",\n     \"what\": \"sell more Oberon-Rubin racks to cover the Kyber gap\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\",\n     \"status_note\": \"as claimed\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i101\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Our roadmap is intact\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"rejects the SemiAnalysis report; says its roadmap (Rubin Ultra / Kyber in 2027) is unchanged\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i197\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\",\n    \"passage\": \"An Nvidia representative responded with a short statement to Tom's Hardware : \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA representative\",\n     \"what\": \"denies the report: roadmap intact\",\n     \"condition\": \"unclear whether the original or an already updated roadmap is meant\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e53 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA's Kyber rack-scale architecture, designed for Rubin Ultra chips, has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis\",\n   \"- e54 [party_statement; NVIDIA, quoted by CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remains intact, rejecting SemiAnalysis's report of a Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\",\n   \"- e55 [rumour; SemiAnalysis, quoted by CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said Kyber NVL144 has been delayed to 2028 because its PCB midplane remains difficult to manufacture.\\n    Quote: \\\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\\\" the firm said\",\n   \"- e58 [third_party_view; SemiAnalysis, quoted by CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA has no proven way to expand Rubin Ultra's scale-up system size and predicted this could give AMD and Google a technical opening in the high-end market.\\n    Quote: That leaves Nvidia with \\\"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\\\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.\",\n   \"- e53 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA's Kyber rack-scale architecture, designed for Rubin Ultra chips, has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e67, e86, e151; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e54 [party_statement; NVIDIA, quoted by CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remains intact, rejecting SemiAnalysis's report of a Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e69; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e55 [rumour; SemiAnalysis, quoted by CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said Kyber NVL144 has been delayed to 2028 because its PCB midplane remains difficult to manufacture.\\n    Quote: \\\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\\\" the firm said\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e131, e136; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e67 [rumour; finance.yahoo.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed NVIDIA's Rubin Ultra high-density rack design, Kyber NVL144, had slipped by more than 12 months because of persistent PCB midplane manufacturing problems.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis claims the high-density rack design built for Rubin Ultra GPUs has slipped by more than 12 months. The firm blamed persistent manufacturing problems with the system's complex PCB midplane.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e53; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e69 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:68a3ed21f77b935d9fa7ec5e 2026-07-06] NVIDIA told media outlets that its roadmap remained intact, rejecting claims of delays and a scrapped rack design.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the claims, telling media outlets that its roadmap remains intact.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e54, e90; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e86 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com, reporting SemiAnalysis’s findings; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA delayed production of its Kyber rack-scale architecture by more than 12 months, moving its release from 2027 to 2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia has delayed production of its Kyber rack-scale architecture by more than 12 months, pushing its release date to 2028, SemiAnalysis has reported.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e53, e130, e142; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e90 [party_statement; NVIDIA spokesperson, quoted by datacenterdynamics.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-06; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] An NVIDIA spokesperson said the company’s roadmap remains intact, responding to DCD’s request for comment on the Kyber claims.\\n    Quote: “Our roadmap is intact.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e69, e139, e158; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e130 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 schedule had slipped by more than twelve months, to 2028, because of manufacturing problems.\\n    Quote: Kyber NVL144, has been pushed back more than twelve months to 2028 because of manufacturing problems.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e86; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e131 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said manufacturing the PCB midplane for NVIDIA's Kyber NVL144 without defects had proved extremely difficult.\\n    Quote: The issue, according to SemiAnalysis, is the circuit boards. Specifically, the PCB midplane, a central board that connects all the individual components, has proven extremely difficult to produce without defects.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e55, e149; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e133 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA canceled the four-compute-die Rubin Ultra version, leaving the two-die version, which it said delivers roughly half the real-world compute performance.\\n    Quote: The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled. Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e138, e156; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e135 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA planned to make up for the Rubin Ultra scale-up shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\\n    Quote: Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\",\n   \"- e136 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack architecture would be delayed to 2028 because of PCB midplane manufacturing challenges.\\n    Quote: Supply chain research firm SemiAnalysis claimed in a weekend report that Nvidia's highly anticipated Kyber NVL144 rack architecture will be delayed to 2028 due to manufacturing challenges with its PCB midplane.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e55; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e139 [party_statement; NVIDIA spokesperson, i