round Nvidia’s next-generation scale-out roadmap and creating a wider competitive window for alternative AI platforms,” he added.\",\n   \"- e151 [rumour; Tom's Hardware; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 rack, intended for Rubin Ultra, is delayed until 2028 from its planned 2027 timing.\\n    Quote: Nvidia reportedly won't ship its Kyber NVL144 rack until 2028, a delay of more than 12 months that pushes the cabinet meant for 2027's Rubin Ultra GPUs into the following year, according to a SemiAnalysis thread on X.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e53; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e156 [rumour; Tom's Hardware; original source Tom's Hardware ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] Tom’s Hardware reported that NVIDIA changed Rubin Ultra from a quad-chiplet to a dual-chiplet GPU the week before publication, halving per-package compute because of manufacturing execution concerns.\\n    Quote: Nvidia dropped the quad-chiplet Rubin Ultra GPU for a dual-chiplet part last week over manufacturing execution concerns, halving the accelerator's per-package compute.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e133; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e157 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:c75f16a6d64cc27fc28fb571 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis assessed that a fully production-ready co-packaged-optics NVSwitch would arrive no earlier than the Feynman generation after Rubin, leaving copper as the near-term Rubin Ultra rack-scale interconnect.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis has also placed a fully production-ready co-packaged optics NVSwitch no earlier than the Feynman generation that follows Rubin, which leaves copper as the only near-term solution for linking Rubin Ultra at rack scale and thereby puts even more weight on the PCB 