ro Devices ( AMD +2.91% ) and Alphabet ( GOOGL -0.36% ) ( GOOG -0.55% ) to gain a foothold in the high end of the AI market.\",\n   \"- e371 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] NVIDIA said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule.\\n    Quote: The company said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e133 (); both are in force: SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA canceled the four-compute-die Rubin Ultra version, leaving the two-die version, which it said delivers roughly half the real-world compute performance.\",\n   \"- e54 [party_statement; NVIDIA, quoted by CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA said its product roadmap remains intact, rejecting SemiAnalysis's report of a Kyber delay.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e69, e172, e254, e355, e467; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e354 [third_party_view; fool.com (Geoffrey Seiler); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:3cd991655d4cdeaa4a578b84 2026-07-12] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 because of manufacturing problems with a crucial circuit board.\\n    Quote: SemiAnalysis reported that its Kyber NVL144 next-gen AI rack system could be delayed until 2028 due to troubles with manufacturing a crucial circuit board.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e136, e466; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e466 [rumour; ebc.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] SemiAnalysis reports circulating over the weekend suggested that NVIDIA’s Kyber NVL144 architecture could be delayed into 2028.\\n    Quote: Over the weekend, reports circulated from industry research firm SemiAnalysis suggesting that Nvidia’s upcoming Kyber NVL144 architecture could face delays extending into 2028.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e354; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e467 [party_statement; ebc.com; original source NVIDIA spokesperson ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] An NVIDIA spokesperson said the company’s roadmap remained intact in response to reports of possible Kyber NVL144 delays.\\n    Quote: Although an Nvidia spokesperson quickly countered the reports, telling that the company's \\\"roadmap is intact,\\\" the seeds of doubt were already sown.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e54; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 22,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"Will Chinese authorities issue any authorization for Chinese companies to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-01-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"Chinese authorities publicly authorize at least one Chinese company to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"Chinese authorities have not publicly authorized any Chinese company to import Nvidia H200 chips by January 31, 2027.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v12\",\n   \"question\": \"By 2026-12-31, will Chinese authorities approve H200 chip imports for named AI companies?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Chinese approvals for importing Nvidia H200 chips\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2026\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"condition\": \"Chinese authorities approve H200 imports for at least one named AI company by 2026-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"No\",\n    \"condition\": \"Chinese authorities have not approved H200 imports for any named AI company by 2026-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i270\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-08\",\n    \"title\": \"China to let AI firms buy Nvidia H200s, says report\",\n    \"passage\": \"China plans to allow top artificial intelligence companies to buy a limited amount of H200 chips from Nvidia\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Chinese officials\",\n     \"what\": \"permission for top AI companies (Alibaba, ByteDance, DeepSeek) to buy NVIDIA H200 chips, each on approval stating the number and reason\",\n     \"how_much\": \"a limited amount; total may be fewer than 200,000\",\n     \"condition\": \"approval per request; limited amount\",\n     \"status\": \"rumour\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i304\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-14\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia slashes list of authorized customers in Asia in a bid to reduce AI chip smuggling, report claims — company sent field inspectors, called customers to check if business is genuine after pressure from Washington\",\n    \"passage\": \"Beijing refused to allow Chinese companies to buy these AI processors\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Beijing\",\n     \"what\": \"Chinese companies not allowed to buy NVIDIA H200\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i305\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-14\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia slashes list of authorized customers in Asia in a bid to reduce AI chip smuggling, report claims — company sent field inspectors, called customers to check if business is genuine after pressure from Washington\",\n    \"passage\": \"all domestic suppliers are sold out and that they’re even considering less powerful chips\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"unnamed Chinese tech executive\",\n     \"what\": \"China's domestic AI-chip suppliers are sold out; buyers are considering less powerful chips\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i309\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-14\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia slashes list of authorized customers in Asia in a bid to reduce AI chip smuggling, report claims — company sent field inspectors, called customers to check if business is genuine after pressure from Washington\",\n    \"passage\": \"President Donald Trump took a 180-degree turn in December 2025 and finally allowed Nvidia to export its H200 GPUs to select customers in the region\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"US President Trump\",\n     \"what\": \"allowed H200 exports to select customers in China\",\n     \"period\": \"December 2025\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e203 [rumour; straitstimes.com; original source The Information 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] Chinese officials reportedly told Alibaba, ByteDance and DeepSeek they would be permitted to purchase some Nvidia H200 chips; the report was published July 8, 2026.\\n    Quote: Chinese officials have informed companies such as Alibaba Group, ByteDance and DeepSeek that they will have permission to purchase some of the processors, which are used to develop AI models, the news site said on July 8 .\",\n   \"- e204 [rumour; straitstimes.com; original source The Information 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] The Information reported that China was still determining the number of H200 chips firms could buy, with the total potentially below 200,000.\\n    Quote: The Chinese government, meanwhile, is still figuring out how many H200 chips to allow the companies to buy, but the total may end up being fewer than 200,000, the Information reported.\",\n   \"- e206 [party_statement; straitstimes.com; original source Nvidia CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] Nvidia CFO Colette Kress said in May 2026 that the company was uncertain whether China would allow any H200 imports.\\n    Quote: “We are uncertain whether any imports will be allowed into the country,” she said.\",\n   \"- e203 [rumour; straitstimes.com; original source The Information 2026-07-08; from gnews:c8c39f971721fd820aab5c1c 2026-07-08] Chinese officials reportedly told Alibaba, ByteDance and DeepSeek they would be permitted to purchase some Nvidia H200 chips; the report was published July 8, 2026.\\n    Quote: Chinese officials have informed companies such as Alibaba Group, ByteDance and DeepSeek that they will have permission to purchase some of the processors, which are used to develop AI models, the news site said on July 8 .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e264, e266; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e264 [rumour; technologyreview.com; original source The Information ; from gnews:50a84fa6b2f3eb33f29948a4 2026-07-09] The Information reported that China plans to permit Alibaba, ByteDance, and DeepSeek to buy Nvidia H200 chips.\\n    Quote: China plans to let its top AI firms buy Nvidia H200 chips\",\n   \"- e265 [fact; South China Morning Post; original source The U.S. government ; from gnews:91684b863d274b10246d0c13 2026-07-09] The U.S. approved H200 exports to China in early 2026.\\n    Quote: In early 2026, Washington took the rare step of approving Nvidia’s H200 graphics processing unit for export to China\",\n   \"- e266 [rumour; An unnamed source with knowledge of the matter, quoted by the South China Morning Post; original source An unnamed source with knowledge of the matter ; from gnews:91684b863d274b10246d0c13 2026-07-09] China plans to let selected companies, including Alibaba, buy limited numbers of Nvidia H200 chips, according to an unnamed source.\\n    Quote: Now, however, China’s stance is beginning to change, as the government plans to let selected companies – including Alibaba Group Holding – buy limited numbers of the device, a source with knowledge of the matter told the South China Morning Post.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e203; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e284 [fact; moomoo.com; original source Chinese authorities ; from gnews:7b39859113d4e2b8ebd8aa86 2026-07-09] China is moving to grant limited approval for domestic firms to buy Nvidia H200 processors, with companies required to seek individual approval for quantities and use cases.\\n    Quote: The stock is also navigating a complex geopolitical environment as China moves to grant limited approval for domestic firms to purchase H200 processors. While this policy shift eases access to Nvidia’s technology, companies must now request individual approval for specific quantities and use cases.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e266 (); both are in force: China plans to let selected companies, including Alibaba, buy limited numbers of Nvidia H200 chips, according to an unnamed source.\",\n   \"- e359 [third_party_view; barchart.com; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] A Bloomberg survey found Chinese technology companies expect domestic suppliers to receive roughly 46% of their AI chip spending over the next year, versus about 30% currently.\\n    Quote: A new Bloomberg survey showed Chinese technology companies expect to allocate roughly 46% of their AI chip spending to domestic suppliers over the next year, up from about 30% currently.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e225; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e386 [party_statement; 247wallst.com, Alex Sirois; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:799ec454c15ddf61f08d042f 2026-07-13] NVIDIA’s Q2 guidance assumes zero Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA leans on scale and CUDA gravity, but assumes zero China Data Center compute revenue in Q2 guidance\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e395; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e395 [fact; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:b68c019528300c6a1fcd3515 2026-07-13] NVIDIA shipped no H20 compute products to China in Q1 FY2027 and excluded Data Center compute revenue from China in its Q2 FY2027 guidance.\\n    Quote: There were no H20 compute products shipped to China in Q1 FY27, and the Q2 FY27 guidance excludes any Data Center compute revenue from China.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e386, e402; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e265 [fact; South China Morning Post; original source The U.S. government ; from gnews:91684b863d274b10246d0c13 2026-07-09] The U.S. approved H200 exports to China in early 2026.\\n    Quote: In early 2026, Washington took the rare step of approving Nvidia’s H200 graphics processing unit for export to China\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e411; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e410 [party_statement; Jeffery Kessler; original source Jeffery Kessler 2026-07-14; from gnews:9d898f2bf43ed52a98e1587a 2026-07-14] Under Secretary of Commerce for Industry and Security Jeffery Kessler said very few H200 and equivalent chips had shipped to China and Hong Kong under issued licenses.\\n    Quote: The bottom line is very few shipments against licenses for H200s and equivalents have taken place. It's a very small quantity of chips,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e419; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e264 (); both are in force: The Information reported that China plans to permit Alibaba, ByteDance, and DeepSeek to buy Nvidia H200 chips.\",\n   \"- e411 [fact; CNBC; original source The U.S. government ; from gnews:9d898f2bf43ed52a98e1587a 2026-07-14] The U.S. government issued licenses for H200 chip exports earlier in 2026.\\n    Quote: Licenses for the chips, which some in the administration say can be used for military purposes, were issued earlier this year .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e265; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e412 [party_statement; Jeffery Kessler; original source Jeffery Kessler 2026-07-14; from gnews:9d898f2bf43ed52a98e1587a 2026-07-14] Jeffery Kessler said the U.S. government reviews H200 export applicants case by case, requiring national-security criteria and compliance inspections.\\n    Quote: Kessler said that the U.S. government assessed companies that want the H200 chips on a case-by-case basis, with applicants needing to meet national security requirements and submit to inspections to make sure the chips are compliant.\",\n   \"- e413 [party_statement; Jeffery Kessler; original source Jeffery Kessler 2026-07-14; from gnews:9d898f2bf43ed52a98e1587a 2026-07-14] Jeffery Kessler said the U.S. government denies some H200 export-license applications.\\n    Quote: \\\"There are cases where we deny the license applications we receive,\\\" Kessler said.\",\n   \"- e419 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source A U.S. commerce official ; from gnews:c73b90b63a733c6ab712fcdd 2026-07-14] A U.S. commerce official told Congress that NVIDIA H200 chip shipments to China had begun, with very few chips shipped so far.\\n    Quote: while the number of H200 chips shipped to China so far was \\\"very few,\\\" the shipments have commenced\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e410; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e433 [fact; Tom's Hardware; original source The Chinese government ; from gnews:2a41a34c16f5280b624481fb 2026-07-14] Beijing reportedly continued to bar Chinese companies from buying NVIDIA H200 GPUs, relying instead on domestic semiconductor suppliers to address the shortfall.\\n    Quote: However, Beijing refused to allow Chinese companies to buy these AI processors — instead, it’s banking on domestic semiconductor manufacturers to make up for the shortfall, but it’s apparently still not enough.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e203 (2026-07-08); both are in force: Chinese officials reportedly told Alibaba, ByteDance and DeepSeek they would be permitted to purchase some Nvidia H200 chips; the report was published July 8, 2026.\",\n   \"- e453 [fact; Reuters; original source U.S. authorities ; from gnews:24268bfaab6ef1d7876b188c 2026-07-14] U.S. authorities permitted ZTE Kangxun Telecom and Maginfra to purchase NVIDIA H200 chips.\\n    Quote: ZTE Kangxun Telecom and server maker Maginfra have been permitted to purchase Nvidia's H200 chips\",\n   \"- e454 [rumour; Reuters, citing two sources familiar with the matter; original source Some Chinese cloud firms, as reported by unnamed sources ; from gnews:24268bfaab6ef1d7876b188c 2026-07-14] Unnamed sources said some Chinese cloud firms recently told partners and clients they may soon be able to obtain NVIDIA H200 chips, indicating progress in Chinese authorities' import reviews.\\n    Quote: some Chinese cloud firms have recently told partners and clients they may soon be able to obtain H200 chips, the sources said, indicating some progress in import reviews by Chinese authorities.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; from pathlib import Path\npts=json.loads(Path(\\\"third-points.json\\\").read_text()); packets=[json.loads(Path(f\\\"controls/control-packet-{n}.json\\\").read_text()) for n in [1,2,4,6,7,9]]\nfor p in pts:\n c=next(x for packet in packets for x in packet if x[\\\"control\\\"]==p[\\\"control\\\"]); print(\\\"\\\\nPOINT\\\",p)\n if p[\\\"field\\\"]==\\\"same_question\\\": print(json.dumps({k:c[k] for k in [\\\"ruler_question\\\",\\\"judged_question\\\",\\\"judged_rungs\\\"]},ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\n else:\n  i=p[\\\"field\\\"].split()[1]; print(\\\"ITEM\\\",json.dumps(next(x for x in c[\\\"reader_b_decisive_items\\\"] if x[\\\"id\\\"]==i),ensure_ascii=False)); print(\\\"EVIDENCE\\\",json.dumps(c[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"],ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; from pathlib import Path\npts=json.loads(Path(\\\"third-points.json\\\").read_text()); packets=[json.loads(Path(f\\\"controls/control-packet-{n}.json\\\").read_text()) for n in [1,2,4,6,7,9]]\nfor p in pts:\n c=next(x for packet in packets for x in packet if x[\\\"control\\\"]==p[\\\"control\\\"]); print(\\\"\\\\nPOINT\\\",p)\n if p[\\\"field\\\"]==\\\"same_question\\\": print(json.dumps({k:c[k] for k in [\\\"ruler_question\\\",\\\"judged_question\\\",\\\"judged_rungs\\\"]},ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\n else:\n  i=p[\\\"field\\\"].split()[1]; print(\\\"ITEM\\\",json.dumps(next(x for x in c[\\\"reader_b_decisive_items\\\"] if x[\\\"id\\\"]==i),ensure_ascii=False)); print(\\\"EVIDENCE\\\",json.dumps(c[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"],ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))'\"","aggregated_output":"\nPOINT {'control': 1, 'field': 'same_question'}\n{\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a guarantee of OpenAI's Ohio data-center lease by 2027-06-30?\",\n    \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-06-30\",\n    \"rungs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Yes\",\n        \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has signed the guarantee by the due day.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"No\",\n        \"condition\": \"It has not.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n    \"view_id\": \"v3\",\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a financial guarantee for OpenAI's lease of the large Ohio data center by December 31, 2027?\",\n    \"looks_at\": \"NVIDIA's reported negotiations to guarantee OpenAI's Ohio data-center lease\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n    \"year\": \"2027\",\n    \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n    {\n      \"position\": 1,\n      \"label\": \"Yes\",\n      \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has signed a financial guarantee for OpenAI's lease of the Ohio data center by December 31, 2027.\",\n      \"lo\": null,\n      \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"position\": 2,\n      \"label\": \"No\",\n      \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not signed a financial guarantee for OpenAI's lease of the Ohio data center by December 31, 2027.\",\n      \"lo\": null,\n      \"hi\": null\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nPOINT {'control': 4, 'field': 'same_question'}\n{\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n    \"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n    \"unit\": \"USD\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n    \"rungs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Below $700 billion\",\n        \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $700 billion.\",\n        \"lo\": null,\n        \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\",\n        \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\",\n        \"lo\": 700000000000.0,\n        \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"$800 billion to below $900 billion\",\n        \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\",\n        \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n        \"hi\": 900000000000.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"$900 billion to below $1000 billion\",\n        \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1000 billion.\",\n        \"lo\": 900000000000.0,\n        \"hi\": 1000000000000.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"$1000 billion or more\",\n        \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1000 billion.\",\n        \"lo\": 1000000000000.0,\n        \"hi\": null\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n    \"view_id\": \"v6\",\n    \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n    \"looks_at\": \"Calendar 2027 data-center capital expenditures by the four largest AI hyperscalers\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n    \"year\": \"2027\",\n    \"kind\": \"theme\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n    {\n      \"position\": 1,\n      \"label\": \"Below $700 billion\",\n      \"condition\": \"Combined spending is below $700 billion.\",\n      \"lo\": null,\n      \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n      \"position\": 2,\n      \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $850 billion\",\n      \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and below $850 billion.\",\n      \"lo\": 700000000000.0,\n      \"hi\": 850000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n      \"position\": 3,\n      \"label\": \"$850 billion to below $1.15 trillion\",\n      \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $850 billion and below $1.15 trillion.\",\n      \"lo\": 850000000000.0,\n      \"hi\": 1150000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n      \"position\": 4,\n      \"label\": \"$1.15 trillion to below $1.3 trillion\",\n      \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1.15 trillion and below $1.3 trillion.\",\n      \"lo\": 1150000000000.0,\n      \"hi\": 1300000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n      \"position\": 5,\n      \"label\": \"$1.3 trillion or more\",\n      \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1.3 trillion.\",\n      \"lo\": 1300000000000.0,\n      \"hi\": null\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nPOINT {'control': 5, 'field': 'same_question'}\n{\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Rubin Ultra generation, in Kyber NVL144 racks, by December 31, 2027?\",\n    \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n    \"rungs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Yes\",\n        \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has begun shipping Rubin Ultra systems by December 31, 2027.\",\n        \"lo\": null,\n        \"hi\": null\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"No\",\n        \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not begun shipping Rubin Ultra systems by December 31, 2027.\",\n        \"lo\": null,\n        \"hi\": null\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n    \"view_id\": \"v8\",\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by December 31, 2028?\",\n    \"looks_at\": \"Whether NVIDIA begins shipping its Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by the end of 2028.\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n    \"year\": \"2028\",\n    \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n    {\n      \"position\": 1,\n      \"label\": \"Yes\",\n      \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has begun shipping the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by 2028-12-31.\",\n      \"lo\": null,\n      \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"position\": 2,\n      \"label\": \"No\",\n      \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not begun shipping the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture by 2028-12-31.\",\n      \"lo\": null,\n      \"hi\": null\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nPOINT {'control': 8, 'field': 'same_question'}\n{\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a guarantee of OpenAI's Ohio data-center lease by 2027-06-30?\",\n    \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-06-30\",\n    \"rungs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Yes\",\n        \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has signed the guarantee by the due day.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"No\",\n        \"condition\": \"It has not.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n    \"view_id\": \"v2\",\n    \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a financial guarantee for OpenAI’s Ohio data-center lease by July 1, 2027?\",\n    \"looks_at\": \"Whether NVIDIA signs a financial guarantee for OpenAI’s Ohio data-center lease\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2027-07-01\",\n    \"year\": \"2027\",\n    \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n    {\n      \"position\": 1,\n      \"label\": \"No\",\n      \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not signed a financial guarantee for the Ohio data-center lease by 2027-07-01.\",\n      \"lo\": null,\n      \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"position\": 2,\n      \"label\": \"Yes\",\n      \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has signed a financial guarantee for the Ohio data-center lease by 2027-07-01.\",\n      \"lo\": null,\n      \"hi\": null\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nPOINT {'control': 12, 'field': 'item i256'}\nITEM {\"id\": \"i256\", \"day\": \"2026-07-07\", \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\", \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\", \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\", \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\", \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\", \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"}}\nEVIDENCE [\n  \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source The four largest AI hyperscalers ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] The four largest AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\",\n  \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source The four largest AI hyperscalers ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] The four largest AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n  \"- e95 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management projected hyperscaler spending of $650 billion in 2026.\\n    Quote: after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e47; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n  \"- e130 [third_party_view; Allen Harris; original source Goldman Sachs ; from gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512 2026-07-06] Goldman Sachs estimated annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026\",\n  \"- e47 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source The four largest AI hyperscalers ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] The four largest AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e95, e184; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n  \"- e184 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author estimates that the four largest AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e47, e192; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n  \"- e192 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author said AI hyperscalers planned $650 billion of data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e184; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n  \"- e205 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Google ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Google guided 2026 capital expenditures to $190 billion.\\n    Quote: 2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion.\",\n  \"- e316 [third_party_view; GuruFocus; original source GuruFocus ; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] Analysts expect overall AI capital expenditures by major cloud service providers to rise significantly, even as NVIDIA's share of Meta's spending may decline.\\n    Quote: However, analysts remain optimistic about NVIDIA's future, suggesting that while its share within Meta may decline, overall AI capital expenditures from major cloud service providers are expected to rise significantly.\",\n  \"- e353 [rumour; tech-insider.org; original source tech-insider.org 2026-07-12; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron reportedly sold out their 2026 HBM output to AI data-center customers.\\n    Quote: The cause is a global memory shortage: Samsung, SK Hynix, and Micron have reportedly sold out their 2026 HBM output to AI data center customers.\",\n  \"- e358 [third_party_view; tech-insider.org, reporting Micron and Kearney’s PERLab; original source Micron and Kearney’s PERLab ; from gnews:8faf69f198e10f14aae67621 2026-07-12] Micron suggested memory supply may not meaningfully normalize until 2027 and may gradually return to balance by 2028; Kearney’s PERLab reportedly projected the shortage could last into 2030.\\n    Quote: Micron has since suggested supply may not meaningfully normalize until 2027, with a gradual return to balance by 2028, while other forecasters take a bleaker view: an analysis from Kearney’s PERLab reportedly projects the shortage could persist into 2030 .\",\n  \"- e421 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Meta raised its 2026 capital expenditure plan to $125–145 billion and launched Meta Compute, a service to rent excess internal AI capacity to enterprises.\\n    Quote: Meta raised 2026 capex to $125 to $145 billion, then quietly launched Meta Compute, a service renting its excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e233 (2026-07-01); both are in force: Bloomberg reported that Meta was setting up a cloud-based business to sell AI compute and models on July 1, 2026.\",\n  \"- e421 [fact; 247wallst.com; original source Meta ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Meta raised its 2026 capital expenditure plan to $125–145 billion and launched Meta Compute, a service to rent excess internal AI capacity to enterprises.\\n    Quote: Meta raised 2026 capex to $125 to $145 billion, then quietly launched Meta Compute, a service renting its excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e460; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e233 (2026-07-01); both are in force: Bloomberg reported that Meta was setting up a cloud-based business to sell AI compute and models on July 1, 2026.\",\n  \"- e434 [third_party_view; fool.com author Justin Pope; original source Meta Platforms, Microsoft, Alphabet and Amazon ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] The author says Meta Platforms, Microsoft, Alphabet and Amazon are planning higher capital expenditures in calendar 2026; no amount is given.\\n    Quote: Hyperscalers, including Meta Platforms , Microsoft , Alphabet , and Amazon , are planning higher capital expenditures in 2026.\",\n  \"- e435 [third_party_view; fool.com author Justin Pope; original source Goldman Sachs ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] Goldman Sachs estimates AI compute spending at approximately $494 billion in calendar 2026, rising to $1.13 trillion by 2031.\\n    Quote: Goldman Sachs estimates that AI compute spending will grow from approximately $494 billion this year to $1.13 trillion by 2031.\",\n  \"- e460 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja; original source 247wallst.com, Vandita Jadeja 2026-07-14; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] The author cited Meta’s $145 billion infrastructure budget, partly aimed at custom silicon, as a potential competitive threat to NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: The Reddit crowd has fixated on competitive threats, from DeepSeek’s rumored in-house chip to Meta’s $145B infrastructure budget aimed partly at custom silicon.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e421; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n  \"- e472 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois), quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the AI-factory buildout was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: Jensen Huang framed the moment bluntly: “The buildout of AI factories, the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e481; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n  \"- e481 [party_statement; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja), quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:184645c8d683d95b684bd6da 2026-07-14] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said AI factory buildout was accelerating at extraordinary speed.\\n    Quote: “The buildout of AI factories , the largest infrastructure expansion in human history, is accelerating at extraordinary speed.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e472; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n  \"- e502 [fact; EBC; original source Amazon ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] Amazon borrowed another $25 billion; EBC said the borrowing caused a minor selloff in AI-related debt.\\n    Quote: Amazon recently made headlines by borrowing another $25 billion, causing a minor selloff in AI-related debt .\"\n]\n\nPOINT {'control': 13, 'field': 'same_question'}\n{\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n    \"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n    \"unit\": \"USD\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n    \"rungs\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Below $700 billion\",\n        \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $700 billion.\",\n        \"lo\": null,\n        \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\",\n        \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\",\n        \"lo\": 700000000000.0,\n        \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"$800 billion to below $900 billion\",\n        \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\",\n        \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n        \"hi\": 900000000000.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"$900 billion to below $1000 billion\",\n        \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1000 billion.\",\n        \"lo\": 900000000000.0,\n        \"hi\": 1000000000000.0\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"$1000 billion or more\",\n        \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1000 billion.\",\n        \"lo\": 1000000000000.0,\n        \"hi\": null\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n    \"view_id\": \"v7\",\n    \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n    \"looks_at\": \"Combined data-center capital expenditures of the four largest AI hyperscalers\",\n    \"due_day\": \"2028-02-29\",\n   